WEBVTT

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:32.993
O'Brien to Sisko.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.465
Go ahead.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:37.095
We've swept all of Level 17.
No sign of the changeling.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:38.104
Move down to 18.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.127
We'll meet you there

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.640
after we finish checking
the guest quarters.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.005
Watch yourself, Chief.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:45.271
This changeling knows
the station as well as we do.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.869
He could be anywhere...
or anything.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.039
Aye, Major.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:00:59.892
We found him!

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.156
He's headed to the Promenade!

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.972
All right, I want phaser sweeps
of everything on the Promenade.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.341
He's here somewhere.
Let's find him.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.471
On three.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.504
One... two...

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.083
Bang. You're dead.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.284
And so is Dr. Bashir.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.123
Computer, elapsed time?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.187
Three hours, 27 minutes.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.528
That's not good enough.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.864
If one of my people were loose
on the station for that long

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.835
there's no telling how much
damage they could do.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.337
Schedule another surprise drill.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.998
If the Dominion tries
to infiltrate the station

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.007
I want to be ready for them.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:49.370
And remind everyone

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.604
that next time, they'd
better sweep everything.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.010
A changeling can be anything...
a post, a pillar

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.014
even a patch
of reflective surfacing.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.175
We get the message, Constable.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.479
I hope so, Chief.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.780
Just remember that the Founders

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.582
are even better shape-shifters
than I am.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.179
Excuse me.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.088
If you're done
scaring my customers away

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.353
I'd like to open the bar.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.723
Go right ahead.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:08.954
Thank you.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.587
Constable...

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.224
it just occurred to me
that, if I knew in advance

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:14.665
just how long it will take

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.169
for them to catch you
during the next drill...

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.568
Well, let's just say

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:21.597
you and I could share
a substantial profit.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.841
Think about it.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.971
Performance reviews
will be held tomorrow

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:29.071
starting at 0800 hours
in the Wardroom.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.980
Check your team leaders
for the schedule.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.517
Dismissed.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.212
How about some dinner?

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.223
Oh, not tonight.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.656
I have a previous engagement.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.658
Oh, that's right...

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.989
Captain Yates got in
this morning.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.186
Give her my regards.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.287
I will.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.795
Come in.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.607
Hello, Ben.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.672
I hope I'm not too late.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:07.482
Some things are
worth waiting for.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.215
Oh...

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.450
Nice...

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:14.392
I'm glad you like it.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.495
For you.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.901
Isn't that a coincidence?

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.496
I have something for you, too.

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.467
Uh...

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:34.810
Oh!

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.543
Where did you find
Tholian silk?

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:42.146
The Tholian Ambassador
owed me a favor.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.849
May I?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.323
It's... not silk

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.848
but I-I think you'll like it.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.326
It's from my brother's team.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:53.491
The Pike City Pioneers.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.967
My brother says if you're
ever on Cestus III

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.300
he'll get you seats
in the dugout.

00:03:58.338 --> 00:03:59.635
How far is Cestus III?

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.699
Eight weeks, at maximum warp.

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.712
To see a real baseball game...

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:09.340
it might be worth the trip.

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:13.216
If you ever decide to go,
I'll take you there myself...

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.721
as long as you don't mind
traveling by freighter.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:18.781
I just might take
you up on that.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.620
Oh!

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.621
Did you do this all yourself?

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:31.194
Well, my father always says
the way to a woman's heart

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.898
is through her stomach.

00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:37.342
So it's my heart you're after.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.072
I never could keep a secret.

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:42.275
In that case, uh,
maybe you could tell me

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.751
what all those maintenance crews
are doing in the docking ring.

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:48.083
Just some retrofitting.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:50.612
Now you are keeping a secret.

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:55.685
Let's just say...
we're preparing a few surprises

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:58.390
just in case the Dominion
comes through the wormhole.

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:01.559
It seems like everyone's
got the Dominion

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.626
on their minds these days.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.605
I hear the Cardassians
have even sealed their borders.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:11.941
What do you say we forget
about... business for a while?

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.980
I'd say that's a good idea.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.151
Dax to Sisko.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:26.386
Go ahead.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.553
I think you'd better
get up here.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.831
On my way.

00:05:38.438 --> 00:05:42.135
I'll be back as...
soon as I can.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.767
I know you will.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:55.878
Benjamin, take a look at this.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:58.083
We've got
some unexpected company.

00:05:58.124 --> 00:06:00.183
It's just de-cloaked.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:02.126
Ah, the new Klingon flagship.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:03.355
The Negh'Var.

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:06.194
There's a General Martok on
board asking to speak with you.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.529
Put him through.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.229
Captain Sisko,
I bring you greetings

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.103
from your allies
in the Klingon Empire.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.199
Welcome to Deep Space 9,
General.

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:18.301
Is there something
I can do for you?

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.312
It has been a long journey.

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.745
My men require shore leave.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:24.477
Certainly. They can come
aboard any time they like.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.041
Good.

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.677
Sowee TAH!

00:08:56.165 --> 00:08:57.928
Oh, Chief...

00:08:57.967 --> 00:08:59.525
I'm beginning to think
there's no limit

00:08:59.569 --> 00:09:00.866
to the wonders you can perform.

00:09:00.903 --> 00:09:03.133
That's what I like about you,
Julian...

00:09:03.172 --> 00:09:05.106
you're easily impressed.

00:09:06.109 --> 00:09:07.303
Thank you, Quark.

00:09:07.343 --> 00:09:09.903
Can we get a little yamok sauce
for these sand peas?

00:09:14.117 --> 00:09:15.345
- Quark?
- Listen.

00:09:15.385 --> 00:09:16.352
Do you hear that?

00:09:17.887 --> 00:09:19.286
I don't hear a thing.

00:09:19.322 --> 00:09:23.520
Exactly. The ambient noise level
in this room

00:09:23.559 --> 00:09:25.584
is less than 30 decibels.

00:09:25.628 --> 00:09:28.119
On an average day, it's 65.

00:09:28.164 --> 00:09:31.361
When there are Klingons in the
room, it can go as high as 85.

00:09:31.401 --> 00:09:34.928
So what you're trying
to say is... it's quiet in here.

00:09:34.971 --> 00:09:36.939
Too quiet.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.735
Something is terribly wrong.

00:09:38.775 --> 00:09:39.799
Well, like what?

00:09:39.842 --> 00:09:40.934
I don't know

00:09:41.044 --> 00:09:44.241
but have you ever met
a quiet Klingon before?

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:48.410
Look how they're watching
the room.

00:09:48.451 --> 00:09:50.146
It's like they're
picking out targets.

00:09:53.523 --> 00:09:56.117
Where are you going?

00:09:56.159 --> 00:09:57.126
Well, I thought

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.491
I'd ask the Klingons
what they're up to.

00:09:58.528 --> 00:09:59.495
Don't do that.

00:09:59.529 --> 00:10:00.621
Why not?

00:10:00.663 --> 00:10:02.824
Because I don't want them
to know we're onto them.

00:10:02.865 --> 00:10:04.059
Well, suit yourself.

00:10:08.071 --> 00:10:12.064
No, the secret is positioning
the pea correctly on the hand.

00:10:12.108 --> 00:10:13.075
But I thought I had that.

00:10:13.109 --> 00:10:14.440
What are you two doing?

00:10:14.477 --> 00:10:17.173
I'm telling you, the Klingons
are up to something.

00:10:17.213 --> 00:10:18.237
Calm down, Quark.

00:10:18.281 --> 00:10:19.714
The Klingons are our allies.

00:10:19.749 --> 00:10:22.980
They might be your allies,
but they're not mine.

00:10:23.019 --> 00:10:24.987
Relax. If there's something up
with the Klingons

00:10:25.054 --> 00:10:26.646
Captain Sisko
will find out about it.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.587
Yeah, but will he tell me?

00:10:31.627 --> 00:10:33.822
So, what brings you here,
General?

00:10:33.863 --> 00:10:35.990
A valid question.

00:10:36.032 --> 00:10:38.091
But first...

00:10:38.134 --> 00:10:41.626
let us be sure we are all
who we say we are.

00:10:51.547 --> 00:10:53.208
You think we're changelings?

00:10:53.249 --> 00:10:56.548
What I think doesn't matter.

00:10:56.586 --> 00:10:59.316
The blood will tell.

00:11:22.011 --> 00:11:23.069
Hmm...

00:11:23.112 --> 00:11:25.740
Now that that's over with...

00:11:25.781 --> 00:11:31.447
We have been sent here to fight
alongside our Federation allies

00:11:31.487 --> 00:11:33.421
against the Dominion.

00:11:33.456 --> 00:11:34.821
I appreciate your gesture

00:11:34.857 --> 00:11:36.916
but I'm not sure it's necessary.

00:11:36.959 --> 00:11:39.951
The Klingon High Council
thinks it is.

00:11:39.996 --> 00:11:42.226
Our communications relay
in the Gamma Quadrant

00:11:42.265 --> 00:11:45.132
hasn't detected any signs
of Jem'Hadar activity

00:11:45.168 --> 00:11:46.533
for quite some time.

00:11:46.569 --> 00:11:49.129
They seem to be giving
the wormhole a wide berth.

00:11:49.172 --> 00:11:51.003
They will come

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:55.374
and when they do,
we will be ready for them.

00:12:06.756 --> 00:12:08.121
Oh, there you are.

00:12:08.157 --> 00:12:10.387
We've been looking
all over for you.

00:12:10.426 --> 00:12:13.156
Malko here just gave me
the most...

00:12:13.196 --> 00:12:15.687
amazing massage

00:12:15.731 --> 00:12:18.393
and I'm sure, if you ask nicely,
he'll do the same for you.

00:12:18.434 --> 00:12:20.595
No, thanks.

00:12:20.636 --> 00:12:22.729
Why?

00:12:22.772 --> 00:12:24.171
Because Malko's not real.

00:12:24.207 --> 00:12:26.675
He's a puppet
made out of holographic light

00:12:26.709 --> 00:12:27.937
and replicated matter.

00:12:27.977 --> 00:12:29.501
Boys...

00:12:29.545 --> 00:12:31.012
can you wait outside?

00:12:36.886 --> 00:12:38.979
Are you afraid I hurt
their feelings?

00:12:39.021 --> 00:12:40.789
Oh, you really should try to get
into the spirit of things.

00:12:40.789 --> 00:12:42.313
Oh, you really should try to get
into the spirit of things.

00:12:42.357 --> 00:12:45.258
People come from all over Trill
to visit the Hoobishan Baths.

00:12:45.293 --> 00:12:47.887
If I'm ever on Trill,
I'm sure I'll visit them

00:12:47.929 --> 00:12:49.863
but we're not on Trill

00:12:49.898 --> 00:12:51.889
and this isn't
the Hoobishan Baths.

00:12:51.933 --> 00:12:54.299
It's a holosuite,
and none of it is real.

00:12:54.335 --> 00:12:55.529
And?

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:57.401
"And"?

00:12:57.438 --> 00:13:01.340
I'm sorry. I feel silly.

00:13:01.376 --> 00:13:04.243
Good! That's
what a holosuite's for...

00:13:04.279 --> 00:13:05.906
to have a good time.

00:13:05.947 --> 00:13:10.247
All you have to do is relax
and use your imagination.

00:13:11.786 --> 00:13:14.118
I guess I don't have
much of an imagination.

00:13:14.155 --> 00:13:17.215
Of course you do.
Everyone does.

00:13:17.258 --> 00:13:21.194
Didn't you play make-believe
when you were a child?

00:13:21.229 --> 00:13:23.663
Yeah. I used to make
believe the Cardassians

00:13:23.698 --> 00:13:25.359
would stop killing the Bajorans

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.594
and just go away.

00:13:26.634 --> 00:13:27.794
I'm sorry, I didn't mean to...

00:13:27.836 --> 00:13:28.962
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

00:13:29.003 --> 00:13:34.703
I... I guess I never had
much use for my imagination.

00:13:34.742 --> 00:13:37.336
I mean, look at me.

00:13:37.378 --> 00:13:39.505
You plan a fun evening for us

00:13:39.547 --> 00:13:43.483
and all I can do is sit here
and worry about Klingons.

00:13:43.518 --> 00:13:45.418
You can worry
about the Klingons tomorrow.

00:13:45.453 --> 00:13:47.921
From what I hear,
they're not going anywhere.

00:13:47.956 --> 00:13:52.120
And as for your underdeveloped
imagination

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:56.824
I prescribe
a strict regime of exercise

00:13:56.865 --> 00:13:58.730
starting immediately.

00:14:00.768 --> 00:14:02.292
All right.

00:14:02.337 --> 00:14:04.430
I'll give it a try.

00:14:04.472 --> 00:14:06.064
That's all I ask.

00:14:06.107 --> 00:14:10.009
Come on. Malko couldn't
have gone far.

00:14:44.812 --> 00:14:48.475
Fascinating.
So both the cup and the liquid

00:14:48.516 --> 00:14:50.279
are merely extensions
of your body.

00:14:50.318 --> 00:14:51.717
That is correct.

00:14:51.753 --> 00:14:54.881
And if I want to,
I can even drink the liquid

00:14:54.923 --> 00:14:56.288
reabsorb it

00:14:56.324 --> 00:15:00.420
and produce new coffee
in the cup.

00:15:09.203 --> 00:15:10.500
This way, I can give

00:15:10.538 --> 00:15:13.439
the illusion that I'm sharing
the dining experience.

00:15:13.474 --> 00:15:15.442
Very thoughtful.

00:15:18.579 --> 00:15:23.676
Tell me, Odo, have you heard
any news from Cardassia lately?

00:15:23.718 --> 00:15:25.948
Not since they sealed
their borders.

00:15:26.054 --> 00:15:29.512
Well, I have, and frankly,
I don't like what I've heard...

00:15:29.557 --> 00:15:31.923
rumors of uprising,
civil disturbance.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.427
It's all very alarming.

00:15:33.461 --> 00:15:37.522
I didn't know you still had
friends inside the Empire.

00:15:37.565 --> 00:15:40.625
One or two, but I can't even
get through to them now.

00:15:40.668 --> 00:15:42.101
That's what worries me.

00:15:42.136 --> 00:15:44.969
With the destruction
of the Obsidian Order

00:15:45.039 --> 00:15:47.132
and the threat of the Dominion

00:15:47.175 --> 00:15:50.576
these are unsettling times
for Cardassia.

00:15:50.611 --> 00:15:51.873
They're unsettling
for everyone...

00:15:51.913 --> 00:15:53.244
Stop!
What are you doing here?

00:15:53.281 --> 00:15:55.306
Let me see that!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:58.148
But if I hear anything,
I'll let you know.

00:15:58.186 --> 00:15:59.983
I'd appreciate that, Constable.

00:16:00.021 --> 00:16:02.148
Excuse me for a moment.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:04.681
...so far away
from the Firelight Nebula.

00:16:04.726 --> 00:16:07.251
So what is it that you
do on this station?

00:16:07.295 --> 00:16:10.162
Can I help you?

00:16:10.198 --> 00:16:13.929
Lohd Zoss-lee chaw-KU
sohk jaTAL?

00:16:14.035 --> 00:16:16.663
Actually, I'm not sure
Constable Odo has a mother.

00:16:16.704 --> 00:16:20.470
Morn, I believe Ensign Saunders
was looking for you.

00:16:20.508 --> 00:16:23.272
Gentlemen, if you have
business on this Promenade

00:16:23.311 --> 00:16:24.938
I suggest you get on with it.

00:16:24.979 --> 00:16:26.810
I'd listen to him,
if I were you.

00:16:26.848 --> 00:16:30.784
I don't take orders
from shape-shifters

00:16:30.818 --> 00:16:33.582
or their Cardassian lapdogs.

00:16:33.621 --> 00:16:35.782
I may be a shape-shifter,
but I am also

00:16:35.823 --> 00:16:37.757
Chief of Security
of this station

00:16:37.792 --> 00:16:38.952
so either move along

00:16:39.027 --> 00:16:41.461
or you'll be continuing
this conversation

00:16:41.496 --> 00:16:43.191
from inside a holding cell.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:48.364
As long as you wear
that Bajoran uniform

00:16:48.403 --> 00:16:50.268
we're allies.

00:16:50.304 --> 00:16:52.829
Make sure you never
take it off.

00:16:58.112 --> 00:16:59.943
I didn't know you spoke Klingon.

00:16:59.981 --> 00:17:03.144
Oh, you'd be surprised
at the things you can learn

00:17:03.184 --> 00:17:05.084
when you're doing alterations.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:21.097
Well, let me guess...

00:17:21.135 --> 00:17:22.602
you're either lost

00:17:22.637 --> 00:17:25.936
or desperately searching
for a good tailor.

00:17:25.973 --> 00:17:27.304
Guess again!

00:17:38.252 --> 00:17:40.311
I can't believe
you're not pressing charges.

00:17:40.354 --> 00:17:43.881
Constable Odo and Captain Sisko
expressed a similar concern.

00:17:43.925 --> 00:17:46.758
But really, Doctor,
there was no harm done.

00:17:46.794 --> 00:17:48.659
They broke seven
of your transverse ribs

00:17:48.696 --> 00:17:50.789
and fractured your clavicle.

00:17:50.832 --> 00:17:52.732
Ah, but I got off
several cutting remarks

00:17:52.767 --> 00:17:56.703
which no doubt did
serious damage to their egos.

00:17:56.737 --> 00:17:57.761
Garak, this isn't funny.

00:17:57.805 --> 00:17:58.772
I'm serious, Doctor.

00:17:58.806 --> 00:17:59.966
Thanks to your ministrations

00:18:00.074 --> 00:18:02.099
I am almost completely healed.

00:18:02.143 --> 00:18:06.580
But the damage I did to them
will last a lifetime.

00:18:06.614 --> 00:18:08.809
What I can't understand

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:12.877
is their inexplicable
hostility toward me.

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.854
Maligning Constable Odo
is one thing...

00:18:14.889 --> 00:18:16.356
after all, he's a changeling.

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.790
The Klingons don't know
him as well as we do.

00:18:18.826 --> 00:18:22.785
But relations between the
Klingon and Cardassian Empires

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:25.492
have never been
anything but amicable.

00:18:25.533 --> 00:18:27.524
With the exception
of the Betreka Nebula Incident.

00:18:27.568 --> 00:18:30.036
A minor skirmish.

00:18:30.071 --> 00:18:31.698
It lasted 18 years.

00:18:31.739 --> 00:18:32.933
It was ages ago.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:37.704
Perhaps they decided
they just didn't like me.

00:18:37.745 --> 00:18:39.042
Not like you?

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.377
Impossible.

00:18:40.414 --> 00:18:42.143
You're right.

00:18:42.183 --> 00:18:45.641
As always, Doctor.

00:18:47.855 --> 00:18:51.723
They must have mistaken me
for someone else.

00:18:51.759 --> 00:18:54.227
The Klingon ships keep
cloaking and de-cloaking

00:18:54.262 --> 00:18:56.526
so it's impossible
to get an exact count

00:18:56.564 --> 00:18:59.192
but so far, we've been
able to identify

00:18:59.233 --> 00:19:00.598
at least 20 different warships

00:19:00.635 --> 00:19:02.535
in the vicinity of the station.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.037
Captain, we're receiving

00:19:04.071 --> 00:19:06.904
a priority one distress call
from the Freighter Xhosa.

00:19:07.008 --> 00:19:08.270
Kasidy's ship?

00:19:08.309 --> 00:19:11.005
She left the station
an hour ago.

00:19:11.045 --> 00:19:12.910
Put her through.

00:19:14.582 --> 00:19:17.449
This is the Freighter Xhosa
to Deep Space 9.

00:19:17.485 --> 00:19:18.816
We're under attack by...

00:19:26.093 --> 00:19:27.583
Her signal's been jammed.

00:19:27.628 --> 00:19:29.425
Get a fix on her location.

00:19:29.463 --> 00:19:31.397
Tell the crew on the Defiant
to man their stations.

00:19:31.432 --> 00:19:33.229
We'll meet you on the Bridge.

00:19:33.267 --> 00:19:34.700
Defiant.

00:19:40.875 --> 00:19:43.036
Forward scanners
are detecting the Xhosa

00:19:43.077 --> 00:19:45.944
at bearing 017 mark 346.

00:19:46.013 --> 00:19:47.640
I'm picking up another ship.

00:19:47.682 --> 00:19:49.843
It's got a tractor beam
on the Xhosa.

00:19:49.884 --> 00:19:51.545
On screen.

00:19:54.589 --> 00:19:56.079
A Klingon ship?

00:19:56.123 --> 00:19:57.954
I can't get through to Kasidy.

00:19:58.025 --> 00:19:59.617
They're still jamming
her communications.

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.685
Hail the Klingon vessel.

00:20:01.729 --> 00:20:04.596
This is Commander Kaybok
of the M'Char.

00:20:04.632 --> 00:20:06.293
What is it you want?

00:20:06.334 --> 00:20:07.961
I want to know
why you stopped that ship.

00:20:08.002 --> 00:20:09.264
We have orders

00:20:09.303 --> 00:20:12.534
to search all vessels attempting
to leave Bajoran space.

00:20:12.573 --> 00:20:13.801
Search them for what?

00:20:13.841 --> 00:20:15.138
For shape-shifters.

00:20:15.176 --> 00:20:17.610
Each ship will be scanned,
its cargo searched

00:20:17.645 --> 00:20:19.613
and its crew members
and passengers

00:20:19.647 --> 00:20:21.615
subjected to genetic testing.

00:20:21.649 --> 00:20:22.911
On whose authority?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.442
On the authority of Gowron
and the Klingon High Council.

00:20:26.487 --> 00:20:28.648
The Klingon High Council
has no jurisdiction

00:20:28.689 --> 00:20:30.179
over ships in Bajoran space.

00:20:30.224 --> 00:20:33.193
We assumed you would welcome
our assistance.

00:20:33.227 --> 00:20:35.991
Do you have any evidence
that there are changelings

00:20:36.063 --> 00:20:37.530
aboard this particular ship?

00:20:37.565 --> 00:20:41.126
How can we have evidence
until we conduct our tests?

00:20:41.168 --> 00:20:45.002
Commander, Bajoran law strictly
prohibits any unwarranted

00:20:45.106 --> 00:20:48.166
search and seizure
of vessels in our territory.

00:20:48.209 --> 00:20:50.268
I have my orders.

00:20:52.713 --> 00:20:55.614
The Klingon ship has increased
power to its tractor beam.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.016
It looks like they're preparing
to board the Xhosa.

00:20:58.119 --> 00:21:00.747
Major, raise shields.

00:21:00.788 --> 00:21:02.415
Power up the forward phasers.

00:21:02.456 --> 00:21:04.686
See if that gets
their attention.

00:21:04.725 --> 00:21:05.692
Shields up.

00:21:05.726 --> 00:21:08.354
Forward phasers standing by.

00:21:10.164 --> 00:21:11.791
They're still not releasing
the tractor beam.

00:21:14.335 --> 00:21:17.498
Fire a warning shot 200 meters
off their starboard bow.

00:21:17.538 --> 00:21:19.972
Yes, sir.

00:21:22.143 --> 00:21:24.134
Commander Kaybok would
like to speak with you.

00:21:24.178 --> 00:21:25.805
Let's hear what he has to say.

00:21:25.846 --> 00:21:28.371
Captain, this is outrageous!

00:21:28.416 --> 00:21:29.713
I agree.

00:21:29.750 --> 00:21:31.513
But you leave me no choice.

00:21:31.552 --> 00:21:33.179
You're violating Bajoran law.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.984
Now, I will ask you
one last time.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.990
Release that ship immediately.

00:21:38.092 --> 00:21:39.389
We are your allies.

00:21:39.427 --> 00:21:42.885
Major, lock phasers
on M'Char's engines.

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:44.898
Prepare to fire on my command.

00:21:44.932 --> 00:21:47.230
Phasers ready.

00:21:50.705 --> 00:21:52.536
K'trek im stram.

00:21:52.573 --> 00:21:54.438
Gowron will hear of this.

00:21:58.746 --> 00:22:01.237
I'm receiving a hail
from the Xhosa.

00:22:01.282 --> 00:22:02.647
It's Captain Yates.

00:22:02.683 --> 00:22:04.742
Put her through.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:07.947
Captain, I don't know
what you said

00:22:07.988 --> 00:22:10.786
to those Klingons
but it must have been good.

00:22:10.825 --> 00:22:12.349
Is everyone all right?

00:22:13.394 --> 00:22:16.557
Everyone is fine.

00:22:18.165 --> 00:22:20.156
I'm glad to hear it.

00:22:20.201 --> 00:22:23.568
We'll keep you on sensors
as long as we can

00:22:23.604 --> 00:22:27.335
but I doubt the Klingons
will give you any more trouble.

00:22:27.375 --> 00:22:28.842
I appreciate that, Captain.

00:22:28.876 --> 00:22:30.969
I'll see you in about two weeks.

00:22:31.045 --> 00:22:33.070
You know where to find me.

00:22:43.324 --> 00:22:45.519
According
to our long-range sensors

00:22:45.559 --> 00:22:47.550
the Klingon task force
has withdrawn

00:22:47.595 --> 00:22:49.529
to just outside
Bajoran territory.

00:22:49.563 --> 00:22:51.861
So now they're
in unclaimed space.

00:22:51.899 --> 00:22:54.527
And if they decide
to continue searching ships...

00:22:54.568 --> 00:22:56.866
There's nothing
we can do about it.

00:22:56.904 --> 00:23:00.135
Unless they try to stop
a Federation or Bajoran vessel.

00:23:00.174 --> 00:23:02.142
Which so far, they haven't done.

00:23:02.176 --> 00:23:05.475
Captain, General Martok
is here to see you.

00:23:05.513 --> 00:23:06.605
Send him in.

00:23:06.647 --> 00:23:07.636
Yes, sir.

00:23:08.816 --> 00:23:10.647
Ah, General.

00:23:10.684 --> 00:23:11.844
We need to talk.

00:23:14.755 --> 00:23:16.484
SOHK-vad.

00:23:29.837 --> 00:23:31.634
It's Commander Kaybok's.

00:23:31.672 --> 00:23:33.469
Why did he give it to me?

00:23:33.507 --> 00:23:36.840
He's letting you know
Kaybok's dead.

00:23:36.877 --> 00:23:40.278
Martok probably had him
executed for disobeying orders.

00:23:40.314 --> 00:23:43.715
Which means,
our next confrontation

00:23:43.751 --> 00:23:47.983
with the Klingons
won't be resolved so easily.

00:23:48.022 --> 00:23:50.650
Any suggestions, old man?

00:23:52.359 --> 00:23:53.986
The longer the Klingons are here

00:23:54.061 --> 00:23:55.858
the worse things
are going to get.

00:23:55.896 --> 00:23:59.662
Whatever you decide to do,
you'd better do it soon.

00:23:59.700 --> 00:24:03.898
Curzon told me once
that, in the long run

00:24:03.938 --> 00:24:07.237
the only people who can
really handle the Klingons

00:24:07.274 --> 00:24:09.640
are Klingons.

00:24:11.312 --> 00:24:13.439
Get me Starfleet Command.

00:24:39.172 --> 00:24:40.799
Commander Worf.

00:24:40.841 --> 00:24:43.366
Chief.
It has been a long time.

00:24:43.410 --> 00:24:44.377
Too long.

00:24:44.411 --> 00:24:45.400
Welcome aboard.

00:24:46.513 --> 00:24:48.743
Just what this station needs...

00:24:48.782 --> 00:24:50.477
another Klingon.

00:24:50.517 --> 00:24:51.506
Come on.

00:25:02.629 --> 00:25:05.393
Lieutenant Commander Worf
reporting for duty, sir.

00:25:08.135 --> 00:25:10.296
It's good to have you aboard,
Commander.

00:25:10.337 --> 00:25:11.804
Thank you, sir.

00:25:11.838 --> 00:25:13.601
At ease, Mr. Worf.

00:25:15.976 --> 00:25:18.945
I was sorry to hear
about the Enterprise.

00:25:18.979 --> 00:25:20.674
She was a good ship.

00:25:20.714 --> 00:25:22.147
Yes, sir.

00:25:22.182 --> 00:25:24.946
I understand you've been
on extended leave.

00:25:24.985 --> 00:25:29.115
Yes, I have been visiting
the Klingon monastery on Boreth.

00:25:29.156 --> 00:25:31.784
I found my discussions
with the clerics there

00:25:31.825 --> 00:25:33.292
to be most enlightening.

00:25:33.327 --> 00:25:34.487
Well, I hope you'll forgive me

00:25:34.528 --> 00:25:36.325
for pulling you
away from your studies

00:25:36.363 --> 00:25:38.957
but I doubt that this assignment
will take very long.

00:25:38.999 --> 00:25:41.058
My leave was almost over, sir.

00:25:41.101 --> 00:25:44.366
Do you have any idea
where you'll be stationed next?

00:25:44.404 --> 00:25:47.134
I am considering resigning
my commission.

00:25:47.174 --> 00:25:48.573
Really?

00:25:48.608 --> 00:25:50.701
May I ask why?

00:25:53.880 --> 00:25:56.872
I have spent
most of my life among humans.

00:25:56.917 --> 00:26:00.182
It has not always been
easy for me.

00:26:02.122 --> 00:26:04.420
And since the destruction
of the Enterprise

00:26:04.458 --> 00:26:07.188
it has become
even more difficult.

00:26:07.227 --> 00:26:10.685
I am no longer sure
I belong in this uniform.

00:26:14.034 --> 00:26:19.336
Mr. Worf, if I told you
we didn't need you here

00:26:19.373 --> 00:26:21.170
I'd be lying

00:26:21.208 --> 00:26:25.668
but if you don't want to take
this assignment, I'd understand.

00:26:25.712 --> 00:26:28.237
Thank you, sir,
but until I make my decision

00:26:28.281 --> 00:26:29.873
I intend to do my duty.

00:26:29.916 --> 00:26:31.406
I'm glad to hear that.

00:26:31.451 --> 00:26:35.080
I assume you've read
my situation report.

00:26:35.122 --> 00:26:36.316
Yes, sir.

00:26:36.356 --> 00:26:38.620
I can't help but feel
that General Martok

00:26:38.658 --> 00:26:41.957
isn't telling the whole truth
about this Klingon task force.

00:26:42.062 --> 00:26:44.394
There are too many
unanswered questions.

00:26:44.431 --> 00:26:46.228
Then I will find you
some answers.

00:26:46.266 --> 00:26:47.290
Good.

00:26:47.334 --> 00:26:48.767
If you need any help,
let me know.

00:26:48.802 --> 00:26:50.531
Yes, sir.

00:26:52.639 --> 00:26:53.833
Commander.

00:26:55.909 --> 00:27:00.141
I once thought about resigning
from Starfleet, too.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:03.240
I know if I had,
I would have regretted it.

00:27:04.518 --> 00:27:07.078
Don't make any quick decisions.

00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:10.419
I will keep that in mind.

00:27:25.539 --> 00:27:28.633
Let me guess...
Klingon bloodwine.

00:27:28.675 --> 00:27:30.336
Prune juice, chilled.

00:27:30.377 --> 00:27:32.038
Prune juice?

00:27:32.078 --> 00:27:34.672
I-lf you say so.

00:27:41.788 --> 00:27:43.915
Commander, over here.

00:27:50.263 --> 00:27:53.960
Dr. Julian Bashir,
Lieutenant Commander Worf.

00:27:54.034 --> 00:27:55.763
Care for a game of darts?

00:27:55.802 --> 00:27:57.292
I do not play games.

00:27:57.337 --> 00:27:59.965
It's like poker,
but with pointed tips.

00:28:01.608 --> 00:28:06.102
All right, think of it
as target practice.

00:28:06.146 --> 00:28:08.137
The object is to throw this dart

00:28:08.181 --> 00:28:10.274
and hit that board over there.

00:28:12.052 --> 00:28:13.644
Aim for the dot in the middle.

00:28:21.294 --> 00:28:22.693
Well, you saw how he was acting!

00:28:22.729 --> 00:28:24.560
I can't believe you did that!

00:28:24.598 --> 00:28:26.190
Well, he didn't
leave me any choice.

00:28:26.233 --> 00:28:27.325
Wait, wait, wait.

00:28:27.367 --> 00:28:28.493
What did she do?

00:28:28.535 --> 00:28:30.400
She knocked out Lancelot.

00:28:30.437 --> 00:28:31.734
He kissed me.

00:28:31.771 --> 00:28:33.602
He's supposed to kiss you.

00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:34.902
But I was playing
a married woman.

00:28:34.941 --> 00:28:36.374
Uh, Lieutenant Commander Worf...

00:28:36.409 --> 00:28:39.503
this is Lieutenant
Commander Jadzia Dax

00:28:39.546 --> 00:28:41.411
and Major Kira Nerys...

00:28:41.448 --> 00:28:44.008
our First Officer.

00:28:46.052 --> 00:28:48.020
Nice hat.

00:28:53.527 --> 00:28:55.085
I, uh...

00:28:55.128 --> 00:28:57.961
I don't usually dress like this.

00:28:59.366 --> 00:29:01.334
We were in the holosuite.

00:29:01.368 --> 00:29:02.630
So I gathered.

00:29:02.669 --> 00:29:05.900
You used to be Curzon Dax.

00:29:05.972 --> 00:29:09.806
That's right, and I don't
usually dress like this either.

00:29:09.843 --> 00:29:13.574
Curzon's name is an honored one
among my people.

00:29:13.613 --> 00:29:16.377
Louk, a jeek CHIM-ta law.

00:29:20.453 --> 00:29:23.183
I suppose so.

00:29:23.223 --> 00:29:24.349
Bartender!

00:29:25.392 --> 00:29:27.087
Bloodwine!

00:29:27.127 --> 00:29:28.492
And hurry!

00:29:31.364 --> 00:29:33.355
Excuse me.

00:29:33.400 --> 00:29:36.369
What did you say to him?

00:29:36.403 --> 00:29:40.931
It loses something
in the translation.

00:29:41.007 --> 00:29:42.941
This bloodwine is cold!

00:29:43.043 --> 00:29:44.772
Get me another one!

00:29:44.811 --> 00:29:49.145
You are Drex, son of Martok.

00:29:51.651 --> 00:29:53.414
That's right.

00:29:53.453 --> 00:29:56.081
I am Worf, son of Mogh.

00:30:12.706 --> 00:30:14.071
He's good.

00:30:14.107 --> 00:30:16.268
What did I tell you?

00:30:36.529 --> 00:30:38.019
Enter.

00:30:40.834 --> 00:30:43.394
I have come
for my son's d'k tahg.

00:30:43.436 --> 00:30:46.405
Give it to me...
or I will take it from you.

00:30:46.439 --> 00:30:49.670
Now that you are here...

00:30:52.212 --> 00:30:54.646
I have no further need of it.

00:30:56.616 --> 00:31:01.485
You robbed my son of his honor
just to get my attention?

00:31:01.521 --> 00:31:04.957
You cannot take away
what someone does not have.

00:31:04.991 --> 00:31:06.549
You're saying my son
is without honor.

00:31:06.593 --> 00:31:09.357
I am saying your son
is a coward and a liar.

00:31:09.396 --> 00:31:10.693
And what of his father?

00:31:11.998 --> 00:31:14.193
That remains to be seen.

00:31:14.234 --> 00:31:20.503
Tell me, what have I done
to earn your disrespect?

00:31:20.540 --> 00:31:24.374
The misdeeds your troops have
committed speak for themselves...

00:31:24.411 --> 00:31:27.437
attacking a Cardassian tailor

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:30.540
detaining and searching ships
in neutral space without warning

00:31:30.583 --> 00:31:34.986
or provocation... and you
executing one of your Commanders

00:31:35.055 --> 00:31:38.752
because he refused
to fire on a Federation ship.

00:31:38.792 --> 00:31:39.986
Whatever we have done

00:31:40.093 --> 00:31:42.891
is in the best interest
of the Alpha Quadrant.

00:31:42.929 --> 00:31:45.591
You must think me a fool to make
your lies so transparent.

00:31:47.300 --> 00:31:50.201
I do not wish to quarrel
with you, Worf.

00:31:50.236 --> 00:31:52.295
Nor I with you.

00:31:52.338 --> 00:31:55.466
The House of Martok
is an honored one

00:31:55.508 --> 00:31:56.998
with a proud tradition

00:31:57.077 --> 00:31:59.443
but I must know
why you are here.

00:31:59.479 --> 00:32:03.313
I am here under the authority
of Gowron himself.

00:32:03.349 --> 00:32:05.442
I am carrying out his orders.

00:32:05.485 --> 00:32:07.385
That should be
all the explanation

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:08.819
a Klingon warrior needs.

00:32:08.855 --> 00:32:12.882
You forget,
I am not only a Klingon warrior

00:32:12.926 --> 00:32:14.826
I am a Starfleet officer

00:32:14.861 --> 00:32:17.125
and Starfleet deserves
an explanation.

00:32:17.163 --> 00:32:20.326
They will get one soon enough.

00:32:20.366 --> 00:32:24.769
Until then, know this:

00:32:24.804 --> 00:32:28.797
My mission will determine

00:32:28.842 --> 00:32:31.072
the fate
of the Klingon Empire.

00:32:31.111 --> 00:32:36.105
Interfere, and you risk
destroying us all.

00:33:05.178 --> 00:33:07.510
You shouldn't drop
your left arm like that.

00:33:07.547 --> 00:33:10.448
I do not remember
asking you for advice.

00:33:10.483 --> 00:33:11.848
I'm just trying to help.

00:33:21.327 --> 00:33:23.454
So, how did you
like the program?

00:33:23.496 --> 00:33:25.054
I found it adequate

00:33:25.098 --> 00:33:27.396
although I was surprised to find

00:33:27.433 --> 00:33:30.698
a Klingon exercise program
on the holosuite.

00:33:30.737 --> 00:33:31.635
It's mine.

00:33:31.671 --> 00:33:33.298
You mean Curzon's.

00:33:33.339 --> 00:33:35.364
No. I mean it's mine.

00:33:35.408 --> 00:33:37.808
Computer, bat'leth.

00:33:37.844 --> 00:33:41.780
I thought you might be tired
of fighting holograms.

00:33:41.814 --> 00:33:43.839
It would not be a fair match.

00:33:46.786 --> 00:33:48.515
I'll go easy on you.

00:33:48.554 --> 00:33:50.181
Very well.

00:33:52.825 --> 00:33:54.520
Defend yourself.

00:34:05.404 --> 00:34:07.372
I hope you're not holding back
because I'm a woman.

00:34:07.406 --> 00:34:09.340
If it makes things any easier,
think of me as a man.

00:34:09.375 --> 00:34:11.400
I've been one several times.

00:34:25.992 --> 00:34:27.721
Feel better?

00:34:29.395 --> 00:34:30.794
I take it your conversation

00:34:30.830 --> 00:34:33.264
with General Martok
didn't go all that well.

00:34:33.299 --> 00:34:37.065
He was not forthcoming,
and he is not the only one.

00:34:38.471 --> 00:34:42.066
I tried to contact
Gowron, Emperor Kahless

00:34:42.108 --> 00:34:44.201
even my brother,
who sits on the High Council.

00:34:44.243 --> 00:34:45.471
No one will speak with me.

00:34:45.511 --> 00:34:47.877
Maybe you're going about this
the wrong way.

00:34:47.914 --> 00:34:49.313
With so many Klingons around

00:34:49.348 --> 00:34:51.908
there must be someone
who owes your family a favor.

00:34:56.823 --> 00:35:00.520
Ej IM-ta fey DE-ja i

00:35:00.560 --> 00:35:04.553
ejadahk-so-TAS
ghos va Skral byteek

00:35:04.597 --> 00:35:08.397
Empa jaj law-moch jaj-pusH

00:35:08.434 --> 00:35:14.771
jaj Kayless Molor-migh
hohk-chew koo.

00:35:19.312 --> 00:35:22.770
Your father and I
used to sing that song

00:35:22.815 --> 00:35:25.784
when you were just a small boy.

00:35:25.818 --> 00:35:30.187
Did I ever tell you how your
father saved my family's honor

00:35:30.223 --> 00:35:33.681
during our blood feud
with the House of Duras?

00:35:33.726 --> 00:35:35.057
Many times.

00:35:35.094 --> 00:35:37.085
It is a good story.

00:35:37.129 --> 00:35:39.120
Yes, and you tell it well.

00:35:39.165 --> 00:35:42.157
Your father was a great warrior.

00:35:42.201 --> 00:35:45.568
My family owes him
everything we have.

00:35:45.605 --> 00:35:50.599
I wish there was some way
I could repay him.

00:35:52.912 --> 00:35:54.971
There is.

00:35:55.014 --> 00:35:57.209
Tell me why the task force
is here

00:35:57.250 --> 00:36:00.947
the real reason, not the one
Martok gave the Federation.

00:36:00.987 --> 00:36:03.421
The real reason?

00:36:03.456 --> 00:36:07.517
I suppose you have
a right to know.

00:36:07.560 --> 00:36:09.653
You are a Klingon warrior

00:36:09.695 --> 00:36:13.631
and it would be wrong
to keep you away from battle.

00:36:15.134 --> 00:36:20.299
And it's going to be
a glorious battle.

00:36:34.253 --> 00:36:37.552
It all seems simpler
from up here, doesn't it?

00:36:40.660 --> 00:36:43.128
If you are looking
to start a conversation

00:36:43.162 --> 00:36:44.390
Iook somewhere else.

00:36:44.430 --> 00:36:46.660
I would prefer to be left alone.

00:36:46.699 --> 00:36:50.829
That may be, but you
can't stay up here forever.

00:36:50.870 --> 00:36:54.101
Sooner or later, you're going to
have to talk to Captain Sisko.

00:36:54.140 --> 00:36:56.904
Whatever it is you've found out
about the Klingons

00:36:56.943 --> 00:36:58.342
he should be the first to know.

00:36:58.377 --> 00:37:01.403
You have been spying on me.

00:37:01.447 --> 00:37:03.472
As Chief of Security

00:37:03.516 --> 00:37:07.418
it's my duty to observe
the inhabitants of this station.

00:37:07.453 --> 00:37:12.049
Since your arrival,
you've transmitted an average

00:37:12.091 --> 00:37:14.355
of five messages a day
to the Klingon Homeworld.

00:37:14.393 --> 00:37:17.487
None of which
has gotten a response.

00:37:17.530 --> 00:37:21.296
Then last night, you met

00:37:21.334 --> 00:37:23.734
with a Klingon officer
in your quarters.

00:37:23.769 --> 00:37:25.930
Since then, you haven't
sent a single message.

00:37:25.972 --> 00:37:27.269
In fact, you've done nothing

00:37:27.306 --> 00:37:29.399
to further your investigation
of the Klingon task force.

00:37:29.442 --> 00:37:31.569
None of which is your business.

00:37:31.610 --> 00:37:35.068
The security of this station
is my business.

00:37:35.114 --> 00:37:37.639
Your behavior
leads me to conclude

00:37:37.683 --> 00:37:40.584
that either you've given up
your investigation

00:37:40.619 --> 00:37:43.179
in which case,
it's my duty to take over

00:37:43.222 --> 00:37:46.555
or... you found something...

00:37:46.592 --> 00:37:49.925
something so disturbing
that you're hesitant

00:37:49.962 --> 00:37:51.554
to inform Captain Sisko.

00:37:54.467 --> 00:37:59.097
I am not interested
in your... conclusions.

00:37:59.138 --> 00:38:00.230
Commander?

00:38:06.979 --> 00:38:09.470
I just wanted to say
that I understand

00:38:09.515 --> 00:38:11.449
what you're going through.

00:38:11.484 --> 00:38:13.782
I've also had to choose
between duty

00:38:13.819 --> 00:38:15.377
and loyalty to my people.

00:38:15.421 --> 00:38:18.185
Yes. I've read
your Starfleet security file.

00:38:18.224 --> 00:38:23.127
Frankly, Mr. Worf, I don't care
which choice you make

00:38:23.162 --> 00:38:25.653
but you owe it to Captain Sisko
to let him know

00:38:25.698 --> 00:38:28.929
which side you're on,
before it's too late.

00:38:30.736 --> 00:38:32.636
Enjoy the view.

00:38:44.850 --> 00:38:47.318
Mr. Worf, what can I do for you?

00:38:47.353 --> 00:38:49.947
Where is Captain Sisko?

00:38:50.056 --> 00:38:52.251
I think he's
in a briefing session with...

00:38:52.291 --> 00:38:54.555
I need to talk to him now.

00:38:54.593 --> 00:38:55.821
Cardassia?

00:38:55.861 --> 00:38:58.694
Why would the Klingons
want to invade Cardassia?

00:38:58.731 --> 00:38:59.891
According to my source

00:38:59.932 --> 00:39:02.799
there has been an uprising
on the Cardassian homeworld.

00:39:02.835 --> 00:39:04.826
The Central Command
has been overthrown

00:39:04.870 --> 00:39:07.270
and power transferred
to civilian authorities.

00:39:07.306 --> 00:39:08.796
Even if your source is correct

00:39:08.841 --> 00:39:11.071
what does that have to do
with the Klingons?

00:39:11.110 --> 00:39:13.169
Gowron and the High
Council believe the coup

00:39:13.212 --> 00:39:14.679
was engineered by the Dominion.

00:39:14.713 --> 00:39:15.907
Do they have any proof?

00:39:15.981 --> 00:39:17.915
None that I know of,
but they are convinced

00:39:17.950 --> 00:39:19.645
that civilians
could not have overthrown

00:39:19.685 --> 00:39:21.084
the Central Command
without help.

00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:24.851
So, by attacking Cardassia,
they think they're protecting

00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:28.519
the Alpha Quadrant
from the Dominion.

00:39:28.561 --> 00:39:29.585
Sisko to Dax.

00:39:29.628 --> 00:39:31.459
Contact General Martok.

00:39:31.497 --> 00:39:33.658
Tell him I need
to meet with him immediately.

00:39:33.699 --> 00:39:35.132
Yes, sir.

00:39:35.167 --> 00:39:37.158
Hmm.

00:39:41.474 --> 00:39:46.275
Mr. Worf, I know this hasn't
been an easy assignment for you.

00:39:46.312 --> 00:39:48.473
No, it has not.

00:39:49.915 --> 00:39:51.405
But I knew this day
would come again

00:39:51.450 --> 00:39:52.610
when I'd be forced to choose

00:39:52.651 --> 00:39:55.211
between the Federation
and the Klingon Empire.

00:39:55.254 --> 00:39:59.554
Maybe you don't have
to make that choice just yet.

00:39:59.592 --> 00:40:01.617
I don't think there's any need

00:40:01.660 --> 00:40:04.652
for you to be there
when I meet with Martok.

00:40:04.697 --> 00:40:06.426
I would prefer to be there.

00:40:06.465 --> 00:40:10.128
I cannot avoid responsibility
for what I have done today.

00:40:15.007 --> 00:40:18.841
I must compliment you on your
intelligence network, Captain.

00:40:18.878 --> 00:40:22.336
One day, you must tell me
how you learned of our plans.

00:40:22.381 --> 00:40:23.348
General...!

00:40:23.382 --> 00:40:25.680
How I got the information
isn't important.

00:40:25.718 --> 00:40:28.710
I think it is,
and so will Gowron.

00:40:28.754 --> 00:40:32.554
General, I want you
to call off this attack.

00:40:32.591 --> 00:40:35.355
And what do you propose
we do instead?

00:40:35.394 --> 00:40:39.194
Stand by and allow the Dominion
to take over the Alpha Quadrant?

00:40:39.231 --> 00:40:42.223
You have no proof that there are
any Founders on Cardassia.

00:40:42.268 --> 00:40:45.369
The change in government
is all the proof we need.

00:40:45.502 --> 00:40:46.833
And what if you are wrong?

00:40:46.870 --> 00:40:50.897
That would be unfortunate...
for the Cardassians.

00:40:50.941 --> 00:40:54.877
General, the Federation Council
has made it clear to me

00:40:54.911 --> 00:40:57.971
that they cannot support
your plans to attack Cardassia.

00:40:59.549 --> 00:41:02.245
Are you saying the Federation
will sit back and do nothing

00:41:02.285 --> 00:41:04.446
while Klingon soldiers
give their lives

00:41:04.488 --> 00:41:06.217
to protect the Alpha Quadrant?

00:41:06.256 --> 00:41:09.589
Starfleet will not participate
in an unprovoked invasion.

00:41:09.626 --> 00:41:12.652
Then the victory
will be ours alone!

00:41:12.696 --> 00:41:16.632
General, I would advise you
to reconsider.

00:41:16.666 --> 00:41:19.191
The Federation Council
has informed Gowron

00:41:19.236 --> 00:41:23.570
that if the attack goes forward,
it will jeopardize our treaty

00:41:23.607 --> 00:41:26.167
with the Klingon Empire.

00:41:26.209 --> 00:41:32.307
Believe me, Captain, we have no
wish to antagonize your people.

00:41:32.349 --> 00:41:34.840
Then call off the attack.

00:41:37.521 --> 00:41:39.716
I will consult with Gowron.

00:41:39.756 --> 00:41:42.554
You will have his decision
within the hour.

00:42:02.546 --> 00:42:05.174
Captain, I think
you better take a look at this.

00:42:08.051 --> 00:42:09.678
Report.

00:42:09.719 --> 00:42:12.347
As soon as General Martok
beamed back to his ship

00:42:12.389 --> 00:42:14.448
he sent a message
to the Klingon fleet.

00:42:14.491 --> 00:42:16.982
It was just one word... "In'Cha. "

00:42:18.829 --> 00:42:20.194
"Begin."

00:42:20.230 --> 00:42:22.289
I'm picking up
a huge distortion wave

00:42:22.332 --> 00:42:23.594
in subspace.

00:42:23.633 --> 00:42:25.658
The Klingon ships
are going to warp.

00:42:25.702 --> 00:42:27.294
Can you plot their course?

00:42:27.337 --> 00:42:29.237
Judging from the vector
on the subspace disturbance

00:42:29.272 --> 00:42:34.676
I'd say their heading is...
269 mark 032.

00:42:34.711 --> 00:42:37.703
Straight
to the Cardassian Empire.

00:42:47.691 --> 00:42:50.990
The Federation Council has been
trying to contact Gowron.

00:42:51.061 --> 00:42:53.325
So far they've had no response.

00:42:53.363 --> 00:42:55.957
So until they've had a chance
to speak with him

00:42:55.999 --> 00:42:58.399
we've been ordered
not to get involved.

00:42:58.435 --> 00:42:59.868
The Bajoran government
has agreed

00:42:59.903 --> 00:43:02.531
to abide by the decisions
of the Federation Council.

00:43:02.572 --> 00:43:04.870
So that means we're not going
to warn the Cardassians?

00:43:04.908 --> 00:43:06.739
The Klingons are
still our allies.

00:43:06.776 --> 00:43:09.768
If we warn the Cardassians,
we'd be betraying them.

00:43:09.813 --> 00:43:12.907
Besides, what if the Klingons
are right?

00:43:12.949 --> 00:43:14.041
What if the Dominion

00:43:14.084 --> 00:43:16.382
has taken over
the Cardassian government?

00:43:16.419 --> 00:43:19.684
If my people wanted to seize
control of Cardassia

00:43:19.723 --> 00:43:21.520
that is how they would do it.

00:43:21.558 --> 00:43:22.855
The coup could have happened

00:43:22.893 --> 00:43:24.588
just as easily
without the Founders.

00:43:24.628 --> 00:43:26.095
The Cardassian
dissident movement

00:43:26.129 --> 00:43:27.756
has been gaining strength
for years.

00:43:27.797 --> 00:43:29.264
With the Obsidian Order
out of the way

00:43:29.299 --> 00:43:31.460
they might have
finally succeeded.

00:43:31.501 --> 00:43:32.866
The issue is not

00:43:32.903 --> 00:43:35.929
if there are any Founders
on Cardassia.

00:43:35.972 --> 00:43:37.132
There are many Klingons

00:43:37.173 --> 00:43:39.141
who say we have been
at peace too long

00:43:39.175 --> 00:43:41.803
that the Empire must expand
in order to survive.

00:43:41.845 --> 00:43:44.746
Fear of the Dominion
has given my people an excuse

00:43:44.781 --> 00:43:46.408
to do what they were born
to do...

00:43:46.449 --> 00:43:48.576
to fight and to conquer.

00:43:48.618 --> 00:43:50.677
If they're so eager to fight

00:43:50.720 --> 00:43:53.587
who's to say they'll stop
with the Cardassians?

00:43:53.623 --> 00:43:56.319
Next target could be anyone,
even the Federation.

00:43:56.359 --> 00:43:59.021
If I were you,
I'd be more worried about Bajor.

00:44:00.063 --> 00:44:01.223
Think about it.

00:44:01.264 --> 00:44:03.459
What good would it do
the Klingons to defeat

00:44:03.500 --> 00:44:05.764
Cardassia if they don't
control the wormhole?

00:44:05.802 --> 00:44:07.292
Agreed.

00:44:07.337 --> 00:44:11.774
If my people return to the
old ways, no one will be safe.

00:44:11.808 --> 00:44:14.368
Then we'll have to make sure
that doesn't happen.

00:44:14.411 --> 00:44:15.742
But how?

00:44:15.779 --> 00:44:18.373
The way I see it,
we only have two choices.

00:44:18.415 --> 00:44:19.643
Both of them bad.

00:44:19.683 --> 00:44:21.776
If we stand by and do nothing

00:44:21.818 --> 00:44:24.685
we run the risk of being
the Klingons' next target.

00:44:24.721 --> 00:44:27.588
But if we disobey Starfleet
orders and warn the Cardassians

00:44:27.624 --> 00:44:30.286
we may end up starting
a war with the Klingons.

00:44:30.327 --> 00:44:34.058
Which means...
we need a third option.

00:44:39.235 --> 00:44:41.430
Trust me, you won't regret this.

00:44:41.471 --> 00:44:42.961
When it comes to keeping warm

00:44:43.039 --> 00:44:44.700
nothing beats
Vitarian wool undergarments.

00:44:44.741 --> 00:44:46.868
And in case you change your mind
about those earmuffs

00:44:46.910 --> 00:44:48.434
I'll keep them on hold for you.

00:44:50.814 --> 00:44:55.183
Mr. Garak, I'd like to see you
in the Wardroom immediately.

00:44:55.218 --> 00:44:56.742
Bring your tailor's kit.

00:44:58.955 --> 00:45:02.083
All together, we're talking
about well over a hundred ships

00:45:02.125 --> 00:45:03.422
just in the first wave.

00:45:03.460 --> 00:45:04.893
Excuse me.

00:45:04.928 --> 00:45:06.122
I hope I'm not interrupting.

00:45:06.162 --> 00:45:07.891
I'd like to be measured
for a new suit.

00:45:07.931 --> 00:45:08.898
Now?

00:45:08.932 --> 00:45:09.921
Right now.

00:45:09.966 --> 00:45:11.627
But, Captain, I do have
your measurements.

00:45:11.668 --> 00:45:12.635
Take them again.

00:45:12.669 --> 00:45:14.762
You were saying, Commander?

00:45:14.804 --> 00:45:17.398
I was saying that between
ground forces and warships

00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:18.668
the Klingons have committed

00:45:18.708 --> 00:45:22.235
almost a third of their
military to this invasion.

00:45:22.278 --> 00:45:23.745
How long before they reach
their target?

00:45:25.682 --> 00:45:26.876
According to our estimates

00:45:26.916 --> 00:45:28.042
the task force should enter

00:45:28.084 --> 00:45:29.517
Cardassian space
within the hour.

00:45:29.552 --> 00:45:30.814
Don't forget the waist.

00:45:30.854 --> 00:45:32.879
I think I've lost
a little weight.

00:45:32.922 --> 00:45:34.514
Well, thank you, Captain.

00:45:34.557 --> 00:45:36.957
I believe
I have everything I need.

00:45:43.333 --> 00:45:45.358
The Klingons?

00:45:45.402 --> 00:45:47.962
Why would the Klingons
invade us?

00:45:48.038 --> 00:45:50.598
According to my sources, the
Klingon High Council believes

00:45:50.640 --> 00:45:53.302
that Cardassia has been
taken over by the Founders.

00:45:53.343 --> 00:45:55.106
That's ridiculous.

00:45:55.145 --> 00:45:56.874
Is it?

00:45:56.913 --> 00:45:58.972
Garak, you have got
to talk to Sisko.

00:45:59.015 --> 00:46:02.644
Tell him he has to find some way
to stop the Klingons.

00:46:02.686 --> 00:46:05.519
Cardassia has enough
problems right now.

00:46:05.555 --> 00:46:08.524
Having trouble
keeping the civilians in line?

00:46:08.558 --> 00:46:11.118
How do you know about that?

00:46:11.161 --> 00:46:14.062
I'm afraid that since the fall
of the Obsidian Order

00:46:14.097 --> 00:46:16.793
Cardassian security
isn't what it used to be.

00:46:16.833 --> 00:46:18.801
Yes.

00:46:18.835 --> 00:46:21.167
Shame about the Order.

00:46:21.204 --> 00:46:24.935
I suppose there won't be
much demand

00:46:24.974 --> 00:46:27.772
for your services anymore.

00:46:27.811 --> 00:46:30.609
Looks like you'll be
hemming women's dresses

00:46:30.647 --> 00:46:32.945
for the rest of your life.

00:46:33.049 --> 00:46:35.677
We can stand here all day
reminding ourselves

00:46:35.719 --> 00:46:37.619
just how much we hate each other

00:46:37.654 --> 00:46:39.588
but you don't have the time.

00:46:39.622 --> 00:46:42.090
The Klingon fleet will reach
Cardassian territory

00:46:42.125 --> 00:46:44.389
in less than one hour.

00:46:44.427 --> 00:46:46.361
I suggest you prepare for them.

00:46:53.536 --> 00:46:55.504
Based on Klingon transmissions

00:46:55.538 --> 00:46:58.530
we've intercepted,
the outlying Cardassian colonies

00:46:58.575 --> 00:47:00.736
were overrun almost immediately.

00:47:00.777 --> 00:47:03.405
But now that the Cardassian
fleet has mobilized

00:47:03.446 --> 00:47:05.380
the Klingons are meeting
stronger resistance.

00:47:05.415 --> 00:47:06.814
You'd almost think
somebody warned

00:47:06.850 --> 00:47:08.215
the Cardassians
they were coming.

00:47:08.251 --> 00:47:10.116
Hopefully, it'll make
the Klingons

00:47:10.153 --> 00:47:11.780
think twice
about what they're doing.

00:47:11.821 --> 00:47:13.550
Unlikely, Major.

00:47:13.590 --> 00:47:16.024
Now that the battle has begun,
Martok and his troops

00:47:16.059 --> 00:47:18.084
will settle for nothing
less than victory.

00:47:25.735 --> 00:47:26.759
Well...

00:47:26.803 --> 00:47:28.634
what did the Federation Council
say?

00:47:28.671 --> 00:47:31.640
They've decided to condemn
the Klingon invasion.

00:47:31.674 --> 00:47:35.610
In response...
Gowron has expelled

00:47:35.645 --> 00:47:38.409
all Federation citizens
from the Klingon Empire

00:47:38.448 --> 00:47:41.645
and recalled his Ambassadors
from the Federation.

00:47:41.684 --> 00:47:44.084
You're saying he cut off
diplomatic relations?

00:47:44.120 --> 00:47:46.418
He's done more than that.

00:47:46.456 --> 00:47:51.086
The Klingons have withdrawn
from the Khitomer Accords.

00:47:51.127 --> 00:47:53.925
The peace treaty
between the Federation

00:47:53.963 --> 00:47:56.955
and the Klingon Empire
has ended.

00:47:57.066 --> 00:47:58.055
Captain.

00:47:59.536 --> 00:48:01.060
You're never going
to believe this.

00:48:01.104 --> 00:48:04.631
A Klingon ship just de-cloaked
off Upper Pylon 3

00:48:04.674 --> 00:48:06.608
and is requesting
permission to dock.

00:48:06.643 --> 00:48:10.340
They claim they have
Chancellor Gowron on board

00:48:10.380 --> 00:48:13.076
and he is demanding
to speak with Mr. Worf...

00:48:13.116 --> 00:48:15.651
personally.

00:48:23.825 --> 00:48:25.793
Chancellor Gowron.

00:48:25.827 --> 00:48:27.317
You wished to speak with me?

00:48:27.362 --> 00:48:29.330
Worf.

00:48:29.364 --> 00:48:32.663
Worf!

00:48:32.701 --> 00:48:34.931
It is good to see you.

00:48:35.003 --> 00:48:36.197
I always said that uniform

00:48:36.238 --> 00:48:37.830
would get you
into trouble one day.

00:48:37.873 --> 00:48:40.706
It seems you were right

00:48:40.742 --> 00:48:42.369
but I do not apologize for my...

00:48:42.411 --> 00:48:44.777
Yes, yes, I know.

00:48:44.813 --> 00:48:46.838
You did what you thought
was right.

00:48:46.882 --> 00:48:49.316
And even though you may
have made some enemies

00:48:49.351 --> 00:48:52.047
I assure you, ha,
I am not one of them.

00:48:52.087 --> 00:48:54.282
I am glad.

00:48:54.322 --> 00:48:56.153
Your friendship
means much to me.

00:48:56.191 --> 00:48:57.453
And yours to me.

00:48:57.492 --> 00:49:01.428
It has been too long since
you last fought at my side.

00:49:01.463 --> 00:49:04.125
Now the time has come again.

00:49:04.166 --> 00:49:07.499
We will do great deeds
in the coming days.

00:49:07.536 --> 00:49:10.562
Deeds worthy of song!

00:49:10.605 --> 00:49:14.041
You want me to go
to Cardassia with you?

00:49:14.076 --> 00:49:16.544
What better way
to redeem yourself

00:49:16.578 --> 00:49:18.546
in the eyes of your people?

00:49:18.580 --> 00:49:20.605
Come with me, Worf.

00:49:20.649 --> 00:49:24.346
Glory awaits you on Cardassia.

00:49:34.463 --> 00:49:38.058
Worf, why do you stand there
like a mute d'blok?

00:49:38.100 --> 00:49:40.068
I have offered you
a chance for glory.

00:49:40.102 --> 00:49:41.729
All you have to do is take it.

00:49:42.738 --> 00:49:45.036
If there's any glory
to be won, Gowron

00:49:45.073 --> 00:49:46.904
it'll have to be yours alone.

00:49:46.942 --> 00:49:48.705
I cannot come with you.

00:49:48.744 --> 00:49:50.803
Of course you can.

00:49:50.846 --> 00:49:52.939
It is where you belong.

00:49:52.981 --> 00:49:55.950
I cannot abandon my post.

00:49:56.017 --> 00:49:57.541
You no longer have a post.

00:49:57.586 --> 00:49:59.110
You have no place
on that station

00:49:59.154 --> 00:50:00.951
and no business
wearing that uniform.

00:50:01.022 --> 00:50:02.785
I have sworn
an oath of allegiance.

00:50:02.824 --> 00:50:03.882
To the Federation!

00:50:03.925 --> 00:50:05.950
You would have me
break my word?

00:50:06.027 --> 00:50:07.688
Your word?

00:50:07.729 --> 00:50:08.889
What good is your word

00:50:08.930 --> 00:50:11.330
when you give it to people
who care nothing for honor?

00:50:11.366 --> 00:50:12.958
Who refuse to lift a finger

00:50:13.001 --> 00:50:16.300
while Klingon warriors
shed blood for their protection?

00:50:16.338 --> 00:50:19.136
I tell you,
they are without honor

00:50:19.174 --> 00:50:22.405
and you do not
owe them anything!

00:50:22.444 --> 00:50:24.605
It is not what I owe them
that matters.

00:50:24.646 --> 00:50:25.977
It is what I owe myself.

00:50:26.081 --> 00:50:28.572
Worf, son of Mogh,
does not break his word.

00:50:28.617 --> 00:50:30.551
And what of your debt to me?

00:50:30.585 --> 00:50:32.382
Are you saying
you owe me nothing?

00:50:32.420 --> 00:50:34.615
I gave you back your name,
restored your house

00:50:34.656 --> 00:50:36.681
gave your family a seat
on the High Council

00:50:36.725 --> 00:50:38.158
and this is how you repay me?

00:50:38.193 --> 00:50:39.182
It is true.

00:50:39.227 --> 00:50:40.819
I owe you a great debt.

00:50:40.862 --> 00:50:44.320
I would give up my life for you.

00:50:44.366 --> 00:50:47.426
But invading Cardassia is wrong,
and I cannot support it.

00:50:47.469 --> 00:50:50.996
Worf... I have
always considered you

00:50:51.072 --> 00:50:53.131
a friend and an ally.

00:50:53.175 --> 00:50:55.609
And because you are my friend

00:50:55.644 --> 00:51:01.207
I am giving you this one
last chance to redeem yourself.

00:51:01.249 --> 00:51:03.274
Come with me.

00:51:05.053 --> 00:51:06.714
I cannot.

00:51:08.523 --> 00:51:10.889
Think about what you are doing.

00:51:10.926 --> 00:51:13.895
If you turn your back on me now

00:51:13.929 --> 00:51:17.592
for as long as I live,
you will not be welcome

00:51:17.632 --> 00:51:19.930
anywhere in the Klingon Empire.

00:51:19.968 --> 00:51:23.699
Your family will be removed
from the High Council

00:51:23.738 --> 00:51:28.072
your lands seized and your House
stripped of its titles!

00:51:28.109 --> 00:51:29.974
You will have nothing!

00:51:33.148 --> 00:51:35.514
Except my honor.

00:51:38.687 --> 00:51:40.655
So be it.

00:51:54.536 --> 00:51:56.697
- Dabo!
- Dabo!

00:52:11.253 --> 00:52:13.483
You look like you could
use some company.

00:52:23.131 --> 00:52:26.294
Chief, do you remember the time

00:52:26.334 --> 00:52:28.666
we rescued Captain Picard
from the Borg?

00:52:28.703 --> 00:52:30.967
How could I forget?

00:52:31.006 --> 00:52:33.531
It was touch and go there
for a while.

00:52:33.575 --> 00:52:35.543
There were a couple of moments

00:52:35.577 --> 00:52:39.308
when I thought we were all going
to wind up being "assimilated."

00:52:39.347 --> 00:52:41.474
Well, I never doubted
the outcome.

00:52:41.516 --> 00:52:44.781
We were like... warriors
from the ancient sagas.

00:52:44.819 --> 00:52:47.151
There was nothing
we could not do.

00:52:47.188 --> 00:52:49.679
Except keep the holodecks
working right.

00:52:56.398 --> 00:53:00.232
I... have decided
to resign from Starfleet.

00:53:00.268 --> 00:53:02.566
Resign?

00:53:02.604 --> 00:53:04.367
What are you talking about?

00:53:04.406 --> 00:53:06.306
I have made up my mind.

00:53:06.341 --> 00:53:07.899
It is for the best.

00:53:07.943 --> 00:53:11.709
Look, I-I know how much
you miss the Enterprise

00:53:11.746 --> 00:53:14.943
but I'm sure they'll be
building a new one soon.

00:53:14.983 --> 00:53:16.507
It will not be the same.

00:53:16.551 --> 00:53:18.678
The Enterprise I knew is gone.

00:53:18.720 --> 00:53:21.951
Now those were good years.

00:53:22.057 --> 00:53:24.548
But now it is time
for me to move on.

00:53:24.592 --> 00:53:25.718
And do what?

00:53:30.332 --> 00:53:32.425
I do not know.

00:53:32.467 --> 00:53:35.163
I thought I would be returning
to Boreth

00:53:35.203 --> 00:53:37.068
but now that is impossible.

00:53:37.105 --> 00:53:38.936
I have made an enemy of Gowron

00:53:38.974 --> 00:53:41.272
and every other Klingon
in the Empire.

00:53:41.309 --> 00:53:44.244
All the more reason
to stay in Starfleet.

00:53:44.279 --> 00:53:46.770
This uniform will only serve
to remind me

00:53:46.815 --> 00:53:50.273
of how I have disgraced myself
in the eyes of my people.

00:53:50.318 --> 00:53:55.415
I suppose I could get a berth
on a Nyberrite Alliance cruiser.

00:53:55.457 --> 00:53:58.392
They are always eager to hire
experienced officers.

00:53:58.426 --> 00:54:00.155
The Nyberrite Alliance?

00:54:00.195 --> 00:54:02.390
That's a long way.

00:54:02.430 --> 00:54:04.022
And what about your son?

00:54:05.700 --> 00:54:07.133
Alexander is much happier

00:54:07.168 --> 00:54:09.261
living with his grandparents
on Earth

00:54:09.304 --> 00:54:11.204
than he ever was
staying with me.

00:54:11.239 --> 00:54:13.799
And one thing is certain...

00:54:13.842 --> 00:54:16.242
the sooner I leave here,
the better.

00:54:16.277 --> 00:54:18.268
My continued presence
on Deep Space 9

00:54:18.313 --> 00:54:20.577
would only be a liability
to Captain Sisko

00:54:20.615 --> 00:54:22.480
in his dealings
with the Klingons.

00:54:22.517 --> 00:54:24.075
Do you hear that, Chief?

00:54:24.119 --> 00:54:27.611
72 decibels.
Music to my ears.

00:54:27.655 --> 00:54:29.680
I think I liked it better
when it was quiet.

00:54:29.724 --> 00:54:32.192
You want quiet,
go to the Replimat.

00:54:32.227 --> 00:54:34.957
This is Quark's
the way Quark's should be

00:54:34.996 --> 00:54:36.861
the way it was meant to be.

00:54:36.898 --> 00:54:40.197
Am I glad we finally got rid
of all those Klingons.

00:54:41.302 --> 00:54:43.930
Uh... present company
excepted, of course.

00:54:50.211 --> 00:54:52.406
I got to hand it to you, Quark.

00:54:52.447 --> 00:54:55.780
You really know how to make
your customers feel welcome.

00:54:57.886 --> 00:54:58.875
What do I care?

00:54:58.920 --> 00:55:01.252
All he ever drinks
is prune juice.

00:55:01.289 --> 00:55:02.916
I'm sorry, Mr. Worf

00:55:03.024 --> 00:55:06.527
but I can't accept
your resignation at this time.

00:55:07.961 --> 00:55:09.758
I do not understand.

00:55:09.796 --> 00:55:11.855
What further use
could I be here?

00:55:11.899 --> 00:55:13.594
I'm not sure yet.

00:55:13.634 --> 00:55:15.534
But as long
as the fighting continues

00:55:15.569 --> 00:55:17.662
between the Klingons
and the Cardassians

00:55:17.704 --> 00:55:19.501
I need you here on the station.

00:55:21.742 --> 00:55:24.108
If you think that is wise.

00:55:25.212 --> 00:55:28.477
I don't know
if it's wise or not.

00:55:28.515 --> 00:55:30.847
But I do know
that you're a good officer

00:55:30.884 --> 00:55:33.944
and right now, I need
every good officer I can get.

00:55:35.489 --> 00:55:38.481
Captain, we just got word
from Bajoran Intelligence.

00:55:38.525 --> 00:55:41.323
The Klingons have broken through
the Cardassian fleet.

00:55:41.361 --> 00:55:44.387
How long before they reach
Cardassia Prime?

00:55:44.431 --> 00:55:45.955
52 hours.

00:55:45.999 --> 00:55:48.832
If the Klingon Empire has
reverted to the old practices

00:55:48.869 --> 00:55:50.700
they will occupy
the Cardassian homeworld

00:55:50.737 --> 00:55:52.170
execute all government officials

00:55:52.205 --> 00:55:54.571
and install an lmperial Overseer

00:55:54.608 --> 00:55:57.076
to put down
any further resistance.

00:55:57.110 --> 00:56:00.705
I think it's about time we had
a talk with the Cardassians.

00:56:00.747 --> 00:56:02.908
Captain, I'm a little busy
at the moment

00:56:02.983 --> 00:56:05.816
so whatever you have to say,
please make it brief.

00:56:05.852 --> 00:56:07.149
Dukat?

00:56:07.187 --> 00:56:10.247
I was trying to reach someone
in the civilian government.

00:56:10.290 --> 00:56:11.917
And you have succeeded.

00:56:12.025 --> 00:56:14.926
You are speaking to the new
Chief Military Advisor

00:56:14.962 --> 00:56:16.259
to the Detapa Council.

00:56:16.296 --> 00:56:19.697
Does this mean you've turned
your back on Central Command?

00:56:19.733 --> 00:56:23.328
It means that as a loyal officer
of the Cardassian military

00:56:23.370 --> 00:56:24.894
I am pledged to serve

00:56:24.938 --> 00:56:27.634
the legitimate ruling body
of the Empire

00:56:27.674 --> 00:56:29.198
whoever that may be.

00:56:29.242 --> 00:56:32.507
In other words, you saw
which way the wind was blowing

00:56:32.546 --> 00:56:34.173
and switched sides.

00:56:34.214 --> 00:56:36.512
It seemed like a good idea
at the time.

00:56:36.550 --> 00:56:39.713
Dukat, you have got to get
those council members to safety

00:56:39.753 --> 00:56:42.278
before the Klingons
reach Cardassia Prime.

00:56:42.322 --> 00:56:44.882
I am open to suggestions,
Captain.

00:56:44.925 --> 00:56:48.417
If you can get a ship
and meet me at these coordinates

00:56:48.462 --> 00:56:51.954
I'll do what I can to escort you
out of the war zone.

00:56:52.032 --> 00:56:55.661
That is a very generous offer.

00:56:55.702 --> 00:56:58.637
I must say I am touched.

00:56:58.672 --> 00:57:01.197
By saving the members
of the Detapa Council

00:57:01.241 --> 00:57:03.141
you will be saving some very...

00:57:03.176 --> 00:57:04.473
Forget the speech, Dukat.

00:57:04.511 --> 00:57:06.206
Just meet me
at the rendezvous point.

00:57:06.246 --> 00:57:08.271
And if the Klingons
try to stop us?

00:57:08.315 --> 00:57:10.112
Then I'll be there
to reason with them.

00:57:10.150 --> 00:57:12.778
I doubt the Klingons
will fire on a Federation ship.

00:57:12.819 --> 00:57:15.413
I'm not sure I share
your optimism.

00:57:15.455 --> 00:57:19.152
But, then, I don't have
much choice, do I?

00:57:19.192 --> 00:57:20.887
We'll meet you there.

00:57:23.630 --> 00:57:26.030
Sir...

00:57:26.066 --> 00:57:27.727
if the Klingons are right...

00:57:27.768 --> 00:57:28.894
if the Cardassian government

00:57:28.935 --> 00:57:30.425
has been taken over
by the Founders...

00:57:30.470 --> 00:57:32.461
Then we'll be helping
them to escape.

00:57:32.506 --> 00:57:34.133
That's the chance
we'll have to take.

00:57:37.678 --> 00:57:40.340
I know you want to be
out of that uniform

00:57:40.380 --> 00:57:43.315
but right now,
I need you with me.

00:57:44.818 --> 00:57:46.183
I understand.

00:57:50.390 --> 00:57:52.153
Make sure the Chief
double-checks

00:57:52.192 --> 00:57:53.318
all our new systems.

00:57:53.360 --> 00:57:54.349
We may need them.

00:57:54.394 --> 00:57:55.793
I'll tell him,
but knowing the Chief

00:57:55.829 --> 00:57:57.057
he's probably doing it already.

00:57:57.097 --> 00:57:58.655
Keep the station
on Yellow Alert.

00:57:58.699 --> 00:58:02.635
And just to be on the safe side,
I'd recommend that you send

00:58:02.669 --> 00:58:05.137
some of the civilian population
down to Bajor.

00:58:05.172 --> 00:58:07.163
I was planning to.

00:58:07.207 --> 00:58:09.471
I wish I was going with you.

00:58:09.509 --> 00:58:10.476
So do I.

00:58:10.510 --> 00:58:12.876
But I need you here.

00:58:16.550 --> 00:58:17.539
Ben!

00:58:19.419 --> 00:58:22.911
I'm, uh... glad I caught you
before you left.

00:58:22.956 --> 00:58:23.923
So am I.

00:58:24.024 --> 00:58:25.013
When'd you get back?

00:58:25.058 --> 00:58:26.855
Uh, less than an hour ago.

00:58:26.893 --> 00:58:31.455
Jake told me you were
about to go off on...

00:58:31.498 --> 00:58:32.931
some kind of mission.

00:58:32.999 --> 00:58:35.490
The Defiant leaves
in a few minutes.

00:58:35.535 --> 00:58:38.197
And you can't tell me
about it.

00:58:38.238 --> 00:58:40.968
I'll be back
in four or five days.

00:58:42.676 --> 00:58:45.076
I'm leaving tomorrow.

00:58:45.112 --> 00:58:47.046
Phew!

00:58:47.080 --> 00:58:50.174
I guess our timing
hasn't been too good.

00:58:50.217 --> 00:58:51.411
No.

00:58:51.451 --> 00:58:53.419
No, it's been terrible.

00:58:53.453 --> 00:58:57.116
I'm not even sure
when I'll be back.

00:58:59.493 --> 00:59:01.393
Make it soon.

00:59:23.950 --> 00:59:26.578
Don't get killed.

00:59:26.620 --> 00:59:28.747
I'll do my best.

00:59:48.041 --> 00:59:49.804
Activate the cloaking device.

00:59:49.843 --> 00:59:52.607
Cloaking device is functioning
within normal parameters.

00:59:54.247 --> 00:59:56.215
Set a course
for the rendezvous point.

00:59:56.249 --> 00:59:57.307
Maximum warp.

00:59:57.350 --> 00:59:59.250
Course laid in.

00:59:59.286 --> 01:00:00.719
Engage.

01:00:00.754 --> 01:00:03.917
Mr. Worf, keep an eye out
for Klingon ships

01:00:03.957 --> 01:00:05.117
cloaked or otherwise.

01:00:05.158 --> 01:00:06.989
Aye, sir.

01:00:09.496 --> 01:00:12.226
Is something wrong, Mr. Worf?

01:00:12.265 --> 01:00:14.927
No, sir.

01:00:14.968 --> 01:00:16.959
Yes, sir.

01:00:17.003 --> 01:00:18.698
It is just...

01:00:18.738 --> 01:00:20.706
I have never been
on a Federation starship

01:00:20.740 --> 01:00:21.968
that had a cloaking device.

01:00:22.075 --> 01:00:24.942
It is... a little strange.

01:00:26.279 --> 01:00:27.803
You'll get used to it.

01:00:31.818 --> 01:00:34.514
Sir, I hate to bring this up

01:00:34.554 --> 01:00:35.851
but our agreement
with the Romulans

01:00:35.889 --> 01:00:37.652
expressly prohibits use
of the cloaking device

01:00:37.691 --> 01:00:38.783
in the Alpha Quadrant.

01:00:38.825 --> 01:00:40.383
You're right, it does.

01:00:40.427 --> 01:00:42.759
But there are hundreds
of Klingon ships

01:00:42.796 --> 01:00:43.990
between us and Dukat

01:00:44.064 --> 01:00:47.261
and I intend to make
that rendezvous in one piece.

01:00:47.300 --> 01:00:49.928
Well, I won't tell the Romulans
if you don't.

01:00:58.578 --> 01:01:00.603
I never thought I'd say this

01:01:00.647 --> 01:01:05.949
but right now...
I'm glad the Dominion's around.

01:01:06.019 --> 01:01:08.681
Otherwise, we never would have
started these upgrades

01:01:08.722 --> 01:01:11.623
let alone have them
almost finished by now.

01:01:11.658 --> 01:01:13.626
Well, there's something to be
said for incentive.

01:01:13.660 --> 01:01:14.820
Uh-huh.

01:01:14.861 --> 01:01:16.761
I just hope everything
works okay.

01:01:16.796 --> 01:01:18.957
You're saying you're not sure?

01:01:18.999 --> 01:01:22.230
The way I see it,
there are two possibilities.

01:01:22.269 --> 01:01:24.362
Either everything
will be fine, or...

01:01:24.404 --> 01:01:25.428
Or?

01:01:25.472 --> 01:01:28.441
Or we'll end up blowing
the station to pieces.

01:01:28.475 --> 01:01:30.409
Oh.

01:01:30.443 --> 01:01:32.570
Well, let's hope
we don't have to find out.

01:01:36.016 --> 01:01:37.142
Captain...

01:01:37.183 --> 01:01:39.344
I am detecting some debris.

01:01:39.386 --> 01:01:43.288
Bearing 025 mark 319.

01:01:43.323 --> 01:01:45.791
Commander, drop us
to one-quarter impulse.

01:01:45.825 --> 01:01:47.588
Aye, Captain.

01:01:47.627 --> 01:01:49.288
It appears to be the wreckage

01:01:49.329 --> 01:01:51.263
of a number
of Cardassian vessels.

01:01:51.298 --> 01:01:52.697
On screen.

01:01:55.869 --> 01:01:58.360
Are there any signs
of survivors?

01:01:58.405 --> 01:02:00.600
I suppose it's possible.

01:02:00.640 --> 01:02:02.801
But there's no way to know
without de-cloaking

01:02:02.842 --> 01:02:04.776
and using our primary
sensor array.

01:02:04.811 --> 01:02:07.439
Sir, I strongly recommend
against that.

01:02:07.480 --> 01:02:09.948
It is likely there are
cloaked Klingon warships

01:02:09.983 --> 01:02:11.610
in the vicinity lying in wait.

01:02:11.651 --> 01:02:14.211
Well, that doesn't sound
very honorable to me.

01:02:14.254 --> 01:02:17.781
In war, there is nothing
more honorable than victory.

01:02:21.094 --> 01:02:24.325
Commander, keep us
at one-quarter impulse...

01:02:24.364 --> 01:02:26.798
until we've cleared
the wreckage.

01:02:26.833 --> 01:02:28.596
Then take us to warp.

01:02:28.635 --> 01:02:31.729
But, sir...
if there are survivors...

01:02:31.771 --> 01:02:33.363
I'm sorry, Doctor,
we can't risk it.

01:02:33.406 --> 01:02:34.498
We have to reach Dukat.

01:02:37.344 --> 01:02:39.505
And double-check the
secondary power grid.

01:02:39.546 --> 01:02:41.878
It's still not performing
as well as it should.

01:02:41.915 --> 01:02:44.150
Yes, sir.

01:02:46.819 --> 01:02:48.218
What's our status?

01:02:48.254 --> 01:02:50.279
We're approaching
the rendezvous point.

01:02:50.322 --> 01:02:54.122
Captain, I am detecting
weapons fire ahead.

01:02:54.160 --> 01:02:56.628
It appears to be three
Klingon birds-of-prey

01:02:56.662 --> 01:02:58.357
attacking a Cardassian vessel.

01:02:58.397 --> 01:03:00.194
The vessel is badly damaged.

01:03:00.232 --> 01:03:01.995
Captain, I'm picking up
a distress signal

01:03:02.034 --> 01:03:03.058
from Dukat, audio only.

01:03:03.102 --> 01:03:04.262
Put it through.

01:03:04.303 --> 01:03:07.170
This is Gul Dukat
of the Cruiser Prakesh.

01:03:07.206 --> 01:03:08.434
We're under heavy fire.

01:03:08.474 --> 01:03:10.169
Our shields are failing.

01:03:10.209 --> 01:03:12.700
I don't know how much longer
we can hold out.

01:03:12.745 --> 01:03:14.906
Send reinforcements immediately.

01:03:14.947 --> 01:03:16.642
I repeat, this is...

01:03:16.682 --> 01:03:18.047
We're in visual range.

01:03:18.083 --> 01:03:19.550
On screen.

01:03:19.585 --> 01:03:21.576
Maximum magnification.

01:03:24.456 --> 01:03:27.357
Two decades of peace
with the Klingons

01:03:27.393 --> 01:03:28.951
and it all comes down to this.

01:03:29.061 --> 01:03:31.825
Orders, Captain.

01:03:37.036 --> 01:03:38.367
Benjamin...

01:03:38.404 --> 01:03:41.396
Dukat's ship isn't going
to last much longer.

01:03:45.177 --> 01:03:47.202
Arm quantum torpedoes...

01:03:47.246 --> 01:03:51.444
drop the cloak,
and raise shields.

01:03:51.483 --> 01:03:53.110
We're going in.

01:04:05.798 --> 01:04:07.095
Red Alert.

01:04:07.132 --> 01:04:08.099
Doctor.

01:04:08.133 --> 01:04:10.863
Commander Worf, transmit
a priority one signal

01:04:10.903 --> 01:04:12.097
to the Klingon ship.

01:04:12.137 --> 01:04:13.695
Tell them to break off
their attack

01:04:13.739 --> 01:04:15.434
and stand down immediately.

01:04:16.942 --> 01:04:18.273
Message sent.

01:04:18.310 --> 01:04:19.777
Captain, I find it
highly unlikely

01:04:19.812 --> 01:04:21.370
that the Klingons
will heed your...

01:04:22.781 --> 01:04:24.749
We've been fired upon
by the lead bird-of-prey.

01:04:24.783 --> 01:04:25.750
Shields are holding.

01:04:25.784 --> 01:04:28.184
I see your point, Mr. Worf.

01:04:28.220 --> 01:04:31.656
Let's show them
what they're up against.

01:04:31.690 --> 01:04:33.920
Attack pattern omega.
Target their engines.

01:04:42.668 --> 01:04:44.568
Incoming message
from the Cardassian ship.

01:04:44.603 --> 01:04:46.002
Put it through.

01:04:50.909 --> 01:04:52.809
I must compliment you, Captain.

01:04:52.845 --> 01:04:55.609
You're nearly Cardassian
in your punctuality.

01:04:55.648 --> 01:04:57.445
Fire phasers!

01:04:57.483 --> 01:04:58.950
Dukat, power up your engines

01:04:58.984 --> 01:05:00.952
and prepare to follow us
back to DS9.

01:05:00.986 --> 01:05:03.546
An excellent suggestion, Captain

01:05:03.589 --> 01:05:06.183
assuming
we had any engines left.

01:05:06.225 --> 01:05:07.419
What's your status?

01:05:09.595 --> 01:05:11.927
Our engines are gone,
our shields are down

01:05:11.997 --> 01:05:13.931
and we have no weapons
to speak of.

01:05:13.999 --> 01:05:15.057
Prepare to evacuate.

01:05:15.100 --> 01:05:17.068
We'll start to beam you over
as soon as possible.

01:05:17.102 --> 01:05:19.730
You'd have to drop your shields
to use your transporters.

01:05:19.772 --> 01:05:21.467
Let me worry about that.
Sisko out.

01:05:28.614 --> 01:05:30.172
Sir, restricting our fire

01:05:30.215 --> 01:05:32.581
to their engines
has not proven effective.

01:05:32.618 --> 01:05:34.609
Very well.
Target at your discretion.

01:05:34.653 --> 01:05:35.915
Aye, aye, sir.

01:05:51.170 --> 01:05:52.194
Dukat's ship is under fire.

01:05:52.237 --> 01:05:53.932
I don't know how much longer
they can hold out.

01:05:53.972 --> 01:05:56.372
Another Klingon ship
has just de-cloaked.

01:05:56.408 --> 01:05:57.932
It is a Vor'cha-class
attack cruiser.

01:05:57.976 --> 01:05:59.944
Sisko to Transporter Bay.

01:05:59.978 --> 01:06:02.538
Stand by to beam aboard
survivors.

01:06:11.156 --> 01:06:12.123
Sisko to Bashir.

01:06:12.157 --> 01:06:13.590
Prepare to receive casualties.

01:06:13.625 --> 01:06:15.820
And, Doctor, have Security
standing by.

01:06:15.861 --> 01:06:18.887
I want our guests
to undergo blood screenings.

01:06:18.931 --> 01:06:19.898
Understood.

01:06:19.932 --> 01:06:21.160
Blood screenings?

01:06:21.200 --> 01:06:23.862
Just in case Martok was right.

01:06:25.170 --> 01:06:27.365
Benjamin, it's going to take
at least two minutes

01:06:27.406 --> 01:06:28.532
to evacuate Dukat's ship.

01:06:28.574 --> 01:06:30.769
Even with the Defiant's
new armor, I don't think

01:06:30.809 --> 01:06:32.834
we can last that long
with our shields down.

01:06:32.878 --> 01:06:33.845
Sir.

01:06:33.879 --> 01:06:35.073
I have a suggestion.

01:06:44.623 --> 01:06:45.954
You were right, Mr. Worf.

01:06:46.024 --> 01:06:47.616
The modulated tractor
beam's deflecting

01:06:47.659 --> 01:06:49.593
some of the Klingon's
disrupter fire.

01:06:49.628 --> 01:06:51.823
Disrupter's effectiveness
at 50 percent.

01:06:51.864 --> 01:06:53.525
Well done, Mr. Worf.

01:06:53.565 --> 01:06:54.759
Lower shields.

01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:56.392
Sisko to Transporter Bay.

01:06:56.435 --> 01:06:58.369
Begin emergency transports.

01:06:58.404 --> 01:06:59.962
Transports underway.

01:07:02.608 --> 01:07:04.235
The ablative armor is holding.

01:07:04.276 --> 01:07:05.834
Klingon ships are closing.

01:07:05.878 --> 01:07:08.847
Armor on the port side
is losing integrity.

01:07:08.881 --> 01:07:11.281
Transporter Bay,
what's our status?

01:07:11.316 --> 01:07:14.114
Captain, this is Dukat.

01:07:14.153 --> 01:07:16.678
Almost half the council members
are still aboard my ship.

01:07:16.722 --> 01:07:19.589
We need at least another minute.

01:07:19.625 --> 01:07:21.058
Looks like we're going
to find out

01:07:21.093 --> 01:07:23.152
just how much of a pounding
this ship can take.

01:07:23.195 --> 01:07:26.358
The Klingons have closed
to point-blank range.

01:07:29.101 --> 01:07:30.329
Ablative armor has failed.

01:07:30.369 --> 01:07:32.735
We've got plasma leaks
on decks 2, 3 and 5.

01:07:32.771 --> 01:07:35.831
And we've lost
our aft torpedo launchers.

01:07:35.874 --> 01:07:36.841
Dukat to Sisko.

01:07:36.875 --> 01:07:38.172
Go ahead.

01:07:38.210 --> 01:07:40.041
The council members are aboard.

01:07:40.078 --> 01:07:41.875
Raise shields.
Activate the cloak.

01:07:41.914 --> 01:07:43.108
Shields up.

01:07:43.148 --> 01:07:46.379
I'm not getting any response
from the cloaking device.

01:07:46.418 --> 01:07:47.715
It's not working.

01:07:47.753 --> 01:07:49.277
Well, that should make
the trip home

01:07:49.321 --> 01:07:50.481
a little more interesting.

01:07:50.522 --> 01:07:53.150
Set a course for DS9,
maximum warp.

01:08:11.743 --> 01:08:13.904
Thank you, Doctor,
but if you don't mind

01:08:13.946 --> 01:08:15.811
I would like to go
to the Bridge now.

01:08:15.848 --> 01:08:17.907
This will only take a minute.
Your arm, please.

01:08:18.016 --> 01:08:19.916
What is the meaning
of this?

01:08:19.952 --> 01:08:21.613
Just a simple blood screening.

01:08:21.653 --> 01:08:24.713
I assure you, Doctor,
I am not a changeling.

01:08:24.756 --> 01:08:26.451
Then you have nothing
to worry about.

01:08:26.492 --> 01:08:28.619
I find this whole
procedure offensive.

01:08:28.660 --> 01:08:29.888
And I find you offensive.

01:08:29.928 --> 01:08:30.895
Now hold up your arm

01:08:30.929 --> 01:08:32.988
or I'll have a Security
Officer do it for you.

01:08:46.311 --> 01:08:48.643
Captain, would
you kindly inform

01:08:48.680 --> 01:08:50.079
this security guard

01:08:50.115 --> 01:08:53.607
that he does not have
to monitor my every move.

01:08:53.652 --> 01:08:55.950
It makes me feel unwelcome.

01:08:55.988 --> 01:08:58.183
Looks like I won, Benjamin.

01:08:58.223 --> 01:08:59.520
You owe me dinner.

01:08:59.558 --> 01:09:02.288
And what is that
supposed to mean?

01:09:02.327 --> 01:09:05.353
Captain Sisko bet me that you
would thank him for the rescue

01:09:05.397 --> 01:09:06.864
before you started
complaining.

01:09:06.899 --> 01:09:08.230
I lost.

01:09:09.835 --> 01:09:14.169
Captain, are you aware
there's a Klingon

01:09:14.206 --> 01:09:15.468
on your Bridge?

01:09:15.507 --> 01:09:18.271
He's not the Klingon you
should be worried about.

01:09:18.310 --> 01:09:22.041
Switch to aft view,
maximum magnification.

01:09:27.586 --> 01:09:29.781
Hmm.

01:09:29.821 --> 01:09:33.416
I'd suggest you cloak
immediately.

01:09:33.458 --> 01:09:35.949
We lost our cloaking device
rescuing you.

01:09:50.309 --> 01:09:53.278
Might I trouble you
for a glass of kanar?

01:09:56.381 --> 01:09:57.541
Help yourself.

01:09:57.583 --> 01:09:58.948
It's on the house.

01:09:59.051 --> 01:10:01.849
Well, how uncharacteristically
generous of you.

01:10:01.887 --> 01:10:03.946
I'm in an uncharacteristic mood.

01:10:03.989 --> 01:10:05.650
Besides, I've got
80 cases of this stuff

01:10:05.691 --> 01:10:06.919
sitting in my stockroom.

01:10:06.959 --> 01:10:09.621
And the way things are going,
I'll never unload another bottle

01:10:09.661 --> 01:10:11.060
unless it's to you.

01:10:11.096 --> 01:10:13.656
How thoughtless of me
not to consider the effects

01:10:13.699 --> 01:10:17.328
the destruction of my homeworld
would have on your business.

01:10:17.369 --> 01:10:20.532
These must be
trying times for you.

01:10:20.572 --> 01:10:21.773
Be brave.

01:10:21.906 --> 01:10:24.238
I should have listened
to my cousin Gaila.

01:10:24.275 --> 01:10:28.109
He said to me, "Quark, I got
one word for you... weapons."

01:10:28.146 --> 01:10:29.613
No one ever went broke

01:10:29.647 --> 01:10:30.909
selling weapons.

01:10:30.948 --> 01:10:32.973
But did I take his advice?

01:10:33.017 --> 01:10:35.315
No.

01:10:35.353 --> 01:10:37.753
And why not?

01:10:37.789 --> 01:10:40.553
Because I'm a people person.

01:10:40.591 --> 01:10:43.651
I like interacting
with my customers

01:10:43.694 --> 01:10:45.685
like you and I are doing
right now.

01:10:45.730 --> 01:10:47.288
Talking to each other

01:10:47.331 --> 01:10:48.923
getting to know one another.

01:10:48.966 --> 01:10:51.958
I can see the attraction
for you.

01:10:52.003 --> 01:10:53.664
But when you're dealing
in weapons

01:10:53.704 --> 01:10:56.104
buyers aren't interested
in casual conversation.

01:10:56.140 --> 01:10:57.971
They just want
their merchandise

01:10:58.009 --> 01:10:59.442
no questions asked.

01:10:59.477 --> 01:11:00.637
So impersonal.

01:11:00.678 --> 01:11:02.908
Your charms would be wasted.

01:11:02.947 --> 01:11:04.574
Exactly.

01:11:06.384 --> 01:11:10.184
So now, Gaila owns his own moon

01:11:10.221 --> 01:11:13.782
and I'm staring into the abyss.

01:11:13.825 --> 01:11:16.089
And the worst part of it is

01:11:16.127 --> 01:11:20.257
my only hope for salvation
is the Federation.

01:11:20.298 --> 01:11:23.392
I know precisely how you feel.

01:11:29.140 --> 01:11:32.200
I want you to try
something for me.

01:11:32.243 --> 01:11:33.733
Take sip of this.

01:11:33.778 --> 01:11:35.075
What is it?

01:11:35.112 --> 01:11:37.171
A human drink.

01:11:37.215 --> 01:11:38.648
It's called root beer.

01:11:38.683 --> 01:11:39.877
I don't know.

01:11:39.917 --> 01:11:40.975
Come on.

01:11:41.052 --> 01:11:43.782
Aren't you just
a little bit curious?

01:11:48.993 --> 01:11:50.517
What do you think?

01:11:50.561 --> 01:11:52.290
It's vile.

01:11:52.330 --> 01:11:53.797
I know.

01:11:53.831 --> 01:11:56.356
It's so bubbly and cloying

01:11:56.400 --> 01:11:58.231
and happy.

01:11:58.269 --> 01:12:01.500
Just like the Federation.

01:12:01.539 --> 01:12:03.666
But you know
what's really frightening?

01:12:03.708 --> 01:12:07.940
If you drink enough of it,
you begin to like it.

01:12:08.045 --> 01:12:10.172
It's insidious.

01:12:10.214 --> 01:12:13.911
Just like the Federation.

01:12:14.919 --> 01:12:18.150
Do you think
they'll be able to save us?

01:12:19.824 --> 01:12:21.815
I hope so.

01:12:23.194 --> 01:12:24.718
- Any luck?
- Not yet.

01:12:25.763 --> 01:12:26.730
Hold on.

01:12:26.764 --> 01:12:29.232
I'm picking up something
on long-range scanners.

01:12:30.234 --> 01:12:31.223
It's the Defiant.

01:12:31.269 --> 01:12:32.236
They made it.

01:12:32.270 --> 01:12:34.738
Yeah, but they've got
two Klingon ships

01:12:34.772 --> 01:12:36.103
on their tail.

01:12:36.140 --> 01:12:38.540
The Captain's hailing us.

01:12:38.576 --> 01:12:40.908
On screen.

01:12:40.945 --> 01:12:42.378
Chief, our ETA
is in five minutes.

01:12:42.413 --> 01:12:43.641
Are the new systems on line?

01:12:43.681 --> 01:12:44.739
Yes, sir.

01:12:44.782 --> 01:12:46.477
I think
we're going to need them.

01:12:46.517 --> 01:12:48.144
I wish we could have
tested them first.

01:12:48.185 --> 01:12:49.812
No time like the present.

01:12:49.854 --> 01:12:51.219
Raise shields.

01:12:51.255 --> 01:12:52.984
Red Alert.

01:12:55.159 --> 01:12:56.353
Now what?!

01:12:56.394 --> 01:12:57.986
Well, I can't be sure, of course

01:12:58.095 --> 01:13:00.086
but my guess would be Klingons.

01:13:00.131 --> 01:13:02.031
The Klingons?

01:13:02.066 --> 01:13:06.093
First, it was the Cardassians,
then it was the Dominion

01:13:06.137 --> 01:13:08.230
now it's the Klingons!

01:13:08.272 --> 01:13:10.604
How's a Ferengi supposed
to make an honest living

01:13:10.641 --> 01:13:11.699
in a place like this?

01:13:21.686 --> 01:13:22.653
Drop out of warp.

01:13:22.687 --> 01:13:24.120
Reverse thrusters at maximum.

01:13:24.155 --> 01:13:25.213
Prepare for docking.

01:13:25.256 --> 01:13:26.223
Aye, sir.

01:13:26.257 --> 01:13:27.952
Well, it looks like the Klingons

01:13:28.059 --> 01:13:30.186
chased us all this way
for nothing.

01:13:30.227 --> 01:13:32.161
That remains to be seen.

01:13:32.196 --> 01:13:34.960
Klingons do not give up easily.

01:13:34.999 --> 01:13:37.263
Two ships against a station?

01:13:37.301 --> 01:13:39.269
I don't think they'd risk it.

01:13:39.303 --> 01:13:41.498
It may not be much of a risk.

01:13:41.539 --> 01:13:42.801
Why do you say that?

01:13:42.840 --> 01:13:44.364
They've got friends.

01:13:56.020 --> 01:13:57.510
Status report, Major.

01:13:57.555 --> 01:13:59.546
I'm detecting
several dozen Klingon ships

01:13:59.590 --> 01:14:00.750
including the Negh'Var.

01:14:00.791 --> 01:14:02.088
They're in an attack formation.

01:14:02.126 --> 01:14:04.424
While you were gone,
we spoke to Starfleet Command.

01:14:04.462 --> 01:14:06.828
They sent a relief force
under Admiral Hastur.

01:14:06.864 --> 01:14:08.126
When will they get here?

01:14:08.165 --> 01:14:09.359
Not soon enough.

01:14:09.400 --> 01:14:11.925
The Klingon ships
have raised their shields

01:14:12.003 --> 01:14:13.368
and charged their weapons.

01:14:13.404 --> 01:14:15.804
What are your orders, Captain?

01:14:20.044 --> 01:14:22.274
Battle stations.

01:14:27.151 --> 01:14:29.517
The thing to remember is
that the Klingons prefer to use

01:14:29.553 --> 01:14:31.680
their knives and bat'leths
in close combat.

01:14:31.722 --> 01:14:34.691
So if we get boarded, you can
expect severe lacerations

01:14:34.725 --> 01:14:37.888
broken bones,
and blunt force traumas.

01:14:37.928 --> 01:14:41.591
All I can say is keep calm,
remember your training...

01:14:41.632 --> 01:14:43.657
and do the best that you can.

01:14:43.701 --> 01:14:44.895
Report to your posts.

01:14:48.839 --> 01:14:50.568
Doctor.

01:14:50.608 --> 01:14:52.371
Constable, what can I
do for you?

01:14:52.410 --> 01:14:54.844
I just wanted you to know
I'll be assigning

01:14:54.879 --> 01:14:57.939
a security unit to the Infirmary
for your protection.

01:14:57.982 --> 01:14:59.813
Well, thank you,
but I'd rather you didn't.

01:14:59.850 --> 01:15:01.613
I'm going to have
wounded people in here.

01:15:01.652 --> 01:15:03.142
The last thing I need
is a team of deputies

01:15:03.187 --> 01:15:05.052
having a fire fight
in my doorway.

01:15:05.089 --> 01:15:06.420
I understand.

01:15:08.125 --> 01:15:09.854
Just do me a favor.

01:15:09.894 --> 01:15:13.057
Don't count on that blue uniform
to protect you.

01:15:13.097 --> 01:15:15.065
In the heat of battle

01:15:15.099 --> 01:15:17.863
Klingons aren't very choosy
about their targets.

01:15:17.902 --> 01:15:18.926
Doctor or no doctor

01:15:19.036 --> 01:15:22.130
you might end up
having to defend yourself.

01:15:22.173 --> 01:15:24.141
Well, hopefully,
it won't come to that.

01:15:24.175 --> 01:15:27.269
But if it does,
I promise you I'll be ready.

01:15:27.311 --> 01:15:28.710
That's all I ask.

01:15:28.746 --> 01:15:30.714
And while we're
on the subject, Constable

01:15:30.748 --> 01:15:32.613
I'm sure there's
more than one Klingon

01:15:32.650 --> 01:15:34.413
who thinks that slaying
a changeling

01:15:34.452 --> 01:15:36.079
would be worthy
of a song or two.

01:15:36.120 --> 01:15:37.883
Doctor, if a Klingon
were to kill me

01:15:37.922 --> 01:15:41.221
I'd expect nothing less than
an entire opera on the subject.

01:15:41.258 --> 01:15:42.953
Maybe.

01:15:43.027 --> 01:15:45.120
I just don't want
to have to listen to it.

01:15:45.162 --> 01:15:46.424
Watch your back.

01:15:56.340 --> 01:15:57.705
Come on, Quark, move it along.

01:15:57.741 --> 01:15:59.834
You should be
in the emergency shelter by now.

01:15:59.877 --> 01:16:01.777
I'm not going
to any emergency shelter.

01:16:01.812 --> 01:16:03.905
This is my bar
and I'm going to defend it.

01:16:03.948 --> 01:16:06.212
Really? And how do
you plan to do that?

01:16:06.250 --> 01:16:07.649
With this.

01:16:07.685 --> 01:16:09.653
You're going to hit
them with a box?

01:16:09.687 --> 01:16:11.245
No. This is my disrupter pistol.

01:16:11.288 --> 01:16:12.653
The one I used to carry
in the old days

01:16:12.690 --> 01:16:14.317
when I was serving
on that Ferengi freighter.

01:16:14.358 --> 01:16:16.121
I thought you were
the ship's cook.

01:16:16.160 --> 01:16:17.422
That's right.

01:16:17.461 --> 01:16:19.622
And every member of that crew
thought he was a food critic.

01:16:19.663 --> 01:16:22.291
If the Klingons try
to get through these doors

01:16:22.333 --> 01:16:24.233
I'll be ready for them.

01:16:24.268 --> 01:16:26.736
"Dear Quark

01:16:26.770 --> 01:16:29.933
"I used parts of your disrupter
to fix the replicators.

01:16:29.974 --> 01:16:31.601
Will return them soon. Rom."

01:16:31.642 --> 01:16:33.769
I will kill him.

01:16:33.811 --> 01:16:35.301
With what?

01:16:59.303 --> 01:17:02.272
That's close enough, Garak.

01:17:02.306 --> 01:17:05.503
I wanted to make sure that
the council members were safe.

01:17:05.543 --> 01:17:08.171
Hoping, no doubt,
that your concern

01:17:08.212 --> 01:17:11.409
would curry
some political favor?

01:17:11.448 --> 01:17:12.745
Oh, and I take it

01:17:12.783 --> 01:17:17.117
your concern is motivated
strictly by patriotism.

01:17:17.154 --> 01:17:20.920
Oh, the council members
are well aware of my patriotism.

01:17:21.025 --> 01:17:25.325
And the sacrifices I was willing
to make in order to save them.

01:17:25.362 --> 01:17:29.731
Now, why don't you go back
to your little tailor shop

01:17:29.767 --> 01:17:32.600
and sew something?

01:17:32.636 --> 01:17:35.537
Because if the Klingons
do invade this station

01:17:35.573 --> 01:17:40.033
you may just need... my help.

01:17:40.077 --> 01:17:42.477
Who would have thought

01:17:42.513 --> 01:17:45.073
that the two of us
would be fighting

01:17:45.115 --> 01:17:47.709
side by side.

01:17:50.154 --> 01:17:52.952
Just remember
when you fire that thing

01:17:53.023 --> 01:17:55.651
you're aiming it at a Klingon.

01:17:55.693 --> 01:17:59.095
I'll try to keep that in mind.

01:18:12.274 --> 01:18:15.243
We're receiving a transmission
from General Martok.

01:18:15.277 --> 01:18:16.904
Put him through.

01:18:16.946 --> 01:18:19.471
Captain, I demand you surrender

01:18:19.515 --> 01:18:22.245
the Cardassian council members
to us immediately.

01:18:22.284 --> 01:18:24.184
They're not Founders, Martok.

01:18:24.220 --> 01:18:25.312
We tested them.

01:18:25.354 --> 01:18:26.480
You were wrong.

01:18:26.522 --> 01:18:29.116
It is of no consequence.

01:18:29.158 --> 01:18:32.457
All that matters is
the Alpha Quadrant will be safer

01:18:32.495 --> 01:18:35.328
with the Klingon Empire
in control of Cardassia.

01:18:35.364 --> 01:18:38.765
Now, surrender
the council members

01:18:38.801 --> 01:18:41.167
or we will have no choice
but to take them by force.

01:18:41.203 --> 01:18:44.536
And risk an all-out war
with the Federation?

01:18:44.573 --> 01:18:47.508
If a war starts here,
the blame will be yours.

01:18:47.543 --> 01:18:49.943
I doubt very much
history will agree.

01:18:50.045 --> 01:18:52.070
History is written
by the victors.

01:18:52.114 --> 01:18:54.082
Consider what you're
doing, Captain.

01:18:54.116 --> 01:18:57.552
The lives of everyone
on your station are at risk.

01:18:57.586 --> 01:18:58.917
I am aware of that.

01:18:58.954 --> 01:19:01.514
But maybe you're not aware
of what you're risking.

01:19:01.557 --> 01:19:03.787
We've had a year
to prepare this station

01:19:03.826 --> 01:19:07.159
for a Dominion attack,
and we're more than ready.

01:19:08.764 --> 01:19:11.289
You're like a toothless
old Grishnar cat

01:19:11.333 --> 01:19:14.427
trying to frighten us
with your roar.

01:19:14.470 --> 01:19:16.097
I can assure you

01:19:16.138 --> 01:19:19.904
this old cat may not be
as toothless as you think.

01:19:19.942 --> 01:19:23.105
Right now, I've got
5,000 photon torpedoes

01:19:23.145 --> 01:19:24.703
armed and ready to launch.

01:19:24.747 --> 01:19:28.410
If you don't believe me,
feel free to scan the station.

01:19:31.820 --> 01:19:33.219
It is a trick.

01:19:33.255 --> 01:19:34.745
An illusion created

01:19:34.790 --> 01:19:37.816
by thoron fields
and duranium shadows.

01:19:37.860 --> 01:19:39.919
It's no illusion.

01:19:40.029 --> 01:19:41.929
We shall see.

01:19:41.997 --> 01:19:45.023
CHEGH-chew jaj-VAM jaj-KAK!

01:19:49.805 --> 01:19:53.502
He said,
"Today is a good day to die."

01:20:14.597 --> 01:20:16.087
Target the lead ships.

01:20:16.131 --> 01:20:18.429
Ready even-numbered
photon launchers.

01:20:18.467 --> 01:20:19.559
Aye, sir.

01:20:30.412 --> 01:20:31.743
Fire on my mark.

01:20:34.149 --> 01:20:35.411
Fire!

01:20:43.525 --> 01:20:45.516
Ready odd-numbered launchers.

01:20:47.896 --> 01:20:48.885
Fire!

01:20:53.035 --> 01:20:54.332
They're still closing.

01:20:54.370 --> 01:20:55.769
Ready phasers.

01:20:55.804 --> 01:20:56.828
Standing by.

01:20:56.872 --> 01:20:57.930
Fire!

01:21:07.149 --> 01:21:08.514
Eight Klingon ships destroyed.

01:21:08.550 --> 01:21:09.642
Several heavily damaged.

01:21:09.685 --> 01:21:10.652
Contact Gowron.

01:21:10.686 --> 01:21:12.517
Maybe we can put an end to this

01:21:12.554 --> 01:21:14.181
before it gets any further.

01:21:16.392 --> 01:21:17.882
They're not responding.

01:21:20.996 --> 01:21:23.464
They have given you
your answer, Captain.

01:21:23.499 --> 01:21:27.993
Weapons stations, fire at will.

01:21:44.987 --> 01:21:47.182
A TLING-on kaogh.

01:21:47.222 --> 01:21:48.484
Zo a TLING-on HegH-lah.

01:21:48.524 --> 01:21:49.923
YoD-wee KAW.

01:21:49.958 --> 01:21:51.323
TIG-mang-Rup.

01:21:51.360 --> 01:21:52.918
Jee-YAJ.

01:21:52.961 --> 01:21:55.896
DuJ-va, YOD-wee-KAW!

01:22:06.375 --> 01:22:09.538
They've disabled
two of our shield generators.

01:22:53.122 --> 01:22:54.646
Thank you, Doctor.

01:22:54.690 --> 01:22:56.214
Any time.

01:22:56.258 --> 01:23:01.355
I find this hand-to-hand combat
really quite distasteful.

01:23:01.397 --> 01:23:02.864
I suppose you prefer
the simplicity

01:23:02.898 --> 01:23:05.093
of an interrogation chamber.

01:23:05.134 --> 01:23:08.297
You have to admit,
it's much more civilized.

01:24:21.210 --> 01:24:22.268
Mr. O'Brien?

01:24:22.311 --> 01:24:23.300
Yeah.

01:24:23.345 --> 01:24:25.279
Get those shields back on line.

01:24:31.086 --> 01:24:32.280
Major?

01:24:32.321 --> 01:24:34.118
I'll be okay.
It's not as bad as it looks.

01:24:34.156 --> 01:24:35.623
Sisko to Odo.

01:24:35.657 --> 01:24:36.681
Odo here.

01:24:36.725 --> 01:24:37.692
Status report.

01:24:37.726 --> 01:24:38.954
We have Klingon troops

01:24:39.061 --> 01:24:40.619
on the Promenade,
the Habitat Ring

01:24:40.662 --> 01:24:41.686
and Lower Pylon Three.

01:24:41.730 --> 01:24:43.254
They seem to be
contained for now

01:24:43.298 --> 01:24:45.289
but I can't guarantee
it'll stay that way.

01:24:45.334 --> 01:24:46.323
Keep me informed.

01:24:48.670 --> 01:24:51.298
There is another wave
of Klingon ships coming in.

01:24:51.340 --> 01:24:52.637
I've got the shields back up

01:24:52.674 --> 01:24:54.505
but I don't know
how long they'll hold.

01:24:54.543 --> 01:24:56.773
I'm reading a cluster
of warp signatures approaching

01:24:56.812 --> 01:24:59.576
bearing 187 mark 025.

01:24:59.615 --> 01:25:00.912
It's Starfleet, Benjamin.

01:25:00.949 --> 01:25:03.144
Six starships
led by the Venture.

01:25:03.185 --> 01:25:04.914
They'll be here in 15 minutes.

01:25:05.020 --> 01:25:07.921
Contact the Negh'Var again.

01:25:08.023 --> 01:25:10.924
Maybe now Gowron will be
in the mood to talk.

01:25:10.959 --> 01:25:12.085
I've got him.

01:25:12.127 --> 01:25:13.856
Captain, your shields

01:25:13.896 --> 01:25:15.420
have been weakened,
your station boarded

01:25:15.464 --> 01:25:17.694
and more Klingon ships
are on their way.

01:25:17.733 --> 01:25:19.200
Surrender while you can.

01:25:19.234 --> 01:25:20.462
I don't think so.

01:25:20.502 --> 01:25:21.901
My shields are holding.

01:25:21.937 --> 01:25:23.928
Your boarding parties
are contained.

01:25:23.972 --> 01:25:26.532
And my reinforcements
are closer than yours.

01:25:26.575 --> 01:25:28.406
You're facing a war
on two fronts.

01:25:28.443 --> 01:25:30.172
Is that what you really want?

01:25:30.212 --> 01:25:31.941
The Empire is not strong enough

01:25:32.047 --> 01:25:34.208
to fight the Federation
and the Cardassians.

01:25:34.249 --> 01:25:36.114
End this now, Gowron

01:25:36.151 --> 01:25:39.382
before you lead the Empire
to its worst defeat in history.

01:25:39.421 --> 01:25:41.412
We will not surrender!

01:25:41.456 --> 01:25:44.391
This is exactly
what the Founders want.

01:25:44.426 --> 01:25:46.417
Klingon against Cardassian.

01:25:46.461 --> 01:25:48.554
Federation against Klingon.

01:25:48.597 --> 01:25:51.589
The more we fight each other,
the weaker we'll get

01:25:51.633 --> 01:25:54.602
and the less chance we have
against the Dominion.

01:25:54.636 --> 01:25:57.127
Consider what you do here,
Gowron.

01:25:57.172 --> 01:25:59.231
Kahless himself said

01:25:59.274 --> 01:26:03.410
"Destroying an Empire
to win a war is no victory."

01:26:03.543 --> 01:26:06.910
"And ending a battle to save
an Empire is no defeat."

01:26:07.013 --> 01:26:08.742
We can still win!

01:26:08.782 --> 01:26:11.876
Not before those Starships
get here.

01:26:11.918 --> 01:26:14.250
Now, what do you want me
to tell them?

01:26:14.287 --> 01:26:18.587
To stand down,
or to come in firing?

01:26:19.959 --> 01:26:22.154
It is we who shall stand down.

01:26:22.195 --> 01:26:24.095
Ach, Gowron, yay chol!

01:26:24.130 --> 01:26:25.097
Enough.

01:26:25.131 --> 01:26:26.098
Cease fire.

01:26:26.132 --> 01:26:27.827
Order our ships
in Cardassian territory

01:26:27.867 --> 01:26:28.856
to halt their advance.

01:26:28.902 --> 01:26:33.202
I do not intend to hand victory
to the Dominion.

01:26:33.239 --> 01:26:34.763
But let your people know

01:26:34.808 --> 01:26:38.437
the Klingon Empire will remember
what has happened here.

01:26:38.478 --> 01:26:41.174
You have sided against us
in battle

01:26:41.214 --> 01:26:47.175
and this, we do not forgive...
or forget.

01:26:52.025 --> 01:26:55.461
The Klingon ships
have powered down their weapons.

01:26:57.130 --> 01:26:58.722
It's over.

01:27:02.335 --> 01:27:04.303
For now.

01:27:06.439 --> 01:27:10.432
Captain's Log, Stardate 49011.4.

01:27:10.477 --> 01:27:13.310
Gowron has returned
to the Klingon Homeworld

01:27:13.346 --> 01:27:16.577
and his task force has withdrawn
from Bajoran space.

01:27:16.616 --> 01:27:19.312
I don't know if I can
fully express the pride I felt

01:27:19.352 --> 01:27:21.411
at seeing how well
Deep Space 9 and its crew

01:27:21.454 --> 01:27:24.082
weathered this latest crisis.

01:27:24.123 --> 01:27:26.387
Though the station
suffered heavy damage

01:27:26.426 --> 01:27:27.893
during the Klingon attack

01:27:27.927 --> 01:27:30.054
repairs are
well ahead of schedule

01:27:30.096 --> 01:27:32.826
and life on the station is
beginning to return to normal

01:27:32.866 --> 01:27:36.962
leaving me with one final piece
of unfinished business.

01:27:51.618 --> 01:27:53.518
Enter.

01:27:55.655 --> 01:27:57.782
I brought your discharge papers.

01:27:57.824 --> 01:27:59.951
I thought you might want
to take a look at them

01:27:59.993 --> 01:28:01.585
before I send them off
to Starfleet.

01:28:01.628 --> 01:28:03.220
Thank you, sir.

01:28:05.265 --> 01:28:09.793
I understand you're headed
for the Nyberrite Alliance.

01:28:09.836 --> 01:28:12.327
Yes, I leave this afternoon.

01:28:13.506 --> 01:28:15.497
For me, it was a job on Earth

01:28:15.542 --> 01:28:18.978
directing construction
of orbital habitats.

01:28:20.947 --> 01:28:22.812
Why did you change your mind?

01:28:22.849 --> 01:28:24.908
I finally realized

01:28:24.951 --> 01:28:28.910
that it wasn't Starfleet
I wanted to get away from.

01:28:29.022 --> 01:28:34.824
I was trying to escape the pain
I felt after my wife's death.

01:28:34.861 --> 01:28:38.490
I thought I could take
the uniform

01:28:38.531 --> 01:28:42.729
wrap it around that pain,
and toss them both away.

01:28:42.769 --> 01:28:46.330
But it doesn't work like that.

01:28:46.372 --> 01:28:49.705
Running may help,
for a little while

01:28:49.742 --> 01:28:53.303
but sooner or later the pain
catches up with you

01:28:53.346 --> 01:28:55.405
and the only way
to get rid of it

01:28:55.448 --> 01:28:59.350
is to stand your ground
and face it.

01:29:01.487 --> 01:29:03.853
But wearing that uniform
must remind you

01:29:03.890 --> 01:29:05.255
of what you have lost.

01:29:05.291 --> 01:29:07.885
Sometimes...

01:29:07.927 --> 01:29:10.896
but it also reminds me
of what I've gained

01:29:10.930 --> 01:29:12.591
and who I am.

01:29:12.632 --> 01:29:15.396
Oh, I can throw away the uniform

01:29:15.435 --> 01:29:18.632
resign my commission,
run all the way

01:29:18.671 --> 01:29:21.640
to the Nyberrite Alliance...

01:29:21.674 --> 01:29:24.268
but it really wouldn't matter.

01:29:24.310 --> 01:29:28.644
A Starfleet Officer...

01:29:28.681 --> 01:29:30.376
that's what I am

01:29:30.416 --> 01:29:32.850
and that's what I'll always be.

01:29:35.755 --> 01:29:37.916
And you think that is true
of me as well.

01:29:37.991 --> 01:29:42.087
What's important, Mr. Worf,
is what you think.

01:29:44.631 --> 01:29:47.964
I think Starfleet has been
my home for many years.

01:29:49.736 --> 01:29:52.500
Perhaps it still is.

01:29:52.538 --> 01:29:55.735
There are starships out there

01:29:55.775 --> 01:29:58.573
that are in need
of good officers.

01:29:58.611 --> 01:30:02.513
In fact, the Captain of
the Venture is a friend of mine.

01:30:02.548 --> 01:30:04.948
If you'd like,
I can talk to him

01:30:04.984 --> 01:30:09.080
see if he has an opening
for a Lieutenant Commander.

01:30:13.192 --> 01:30:16.423
Perhaps that
will not be necessary.

01:30:27.340 --> 01:30:28.637
Lieutenant Commander Worf

01:30:28.675 --> 01:30:30.700
reporting for duty, sir.

01:30:30.743 --> 01:30:34.770
Well, you all know our new
Strategic Operations Officer.

01:30:34.814 --> 01:30:35.781
Commander.

01:30:35.815 --> 01:30:36.804
Glad you're here.

01:30:36.849 --> 01:30:37.975
Thank you.
Thank you.

01:30:38.084 --> 01:30:38.982
Congratulations.

01:30:39.085 --> 01:30:41.451
Assume your post, Mr. Worf.

01:30:41.487 --> 01:30:42.681
Yes, sir.

01:30:44.257 --> 01:30:46.919
You look good in red.

01:30:46.959 --> 01:30:48.620
It feels good.

01:30:48.661 --> 01:30:51.721
But I have a lot to learn
about command.

01:30:51.764 --> 01:30:54.289
Well, you couldn't ask
for a better teacher.

01:30:57.070 --> 01:30:59.937
Now that everyone is here,
I wanted you to know

01:30:59.972 --> 01:31:01.337
I've spoken with Dukat

01:31:01.374 --> 01:31:03.934
and several members
of the Detapa Council.

01:31:03.976 --> 01:31:07.139
They've returned to Cardassia
Prime without incident

01:31:07.180 --> 01:31:10.445
and wanted me to convey to you
their personal thanks.

01:31:11.984 --> 01:31:14.544
Who'd have thought I'd help
save the Cardassian government?

01:31:14.587 --> 01:31:15.815
Don't worry.

01:31:15.855 --> 01:31:18.824
I'm sure Gul Dukat
will take all the credit.

01:31:18.858 --> 01:31:20.519
Poor Garak... Dukat's a hero

01:31:20.560 --> 01:31:24.326
and Garak's still stuck in his
tailor shop hemming trousers.

01:31:24.363 --> 01:31:27.389
Captain, I'm receiving
a priority one message

01:31:27.433 --> 01:31:29.128
from Starfleet Intelligence.

01:31:29.168 --> 01:31:31.295
The Klingons are refusing
to give up

01:31:31.337 --> 01:31:33.396
several
of the Cardassian colonies

01:31:33.439 --> 01:31:35.373
they seized during the invasion.

01:31:35.408 --> 01:31:37.603
They're fortifying
their positions

01:31:37.643 --> 01:31:40.635
and deploying
orbital defense systems.

01:31:40.680 --> 01:31:43.649
Looks like the Klingons
are here to stay.

01:31:50.356 --> 01:31:52.187
Maybe they are...

01:31:53.860 --> 01:31:55.691
but so are we.
